{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped","id":1377947,"title":"Heirs To The Shogunate Backers Preview just dropped","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-02T08:18:15-07:00","id":1377947,"title":"Heirs To The Shogunate Backers Preview just dropped","content":"For those of us out there who have puzzled over some of the more troublesome aspect v abilities match-ups (looking at <i>you</i> air melee-ist), at a very quick glance, all I can say is... squee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-02-2020, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:27:04-07:00","id":1377952,"title":"","content":"It's quite exciting to have my backer Charm finally see the light of day. This preview really saves the best for last. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I asked for something like Tepet Arada would use, that reflected his specialization in fast attacks. I really like how it turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:36:24-07:00","id":1377954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377952#post1377952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's quite exciting to have my backer Charm finally see the light of day. This preview really saves the best for last. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I asked for something like Tepet Arada would use, that reflected his specialization in fast attacks. I really like how it turned out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice work!<br /> <br /> Feel like air has gotten a lot of love so far...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:38:02-07:00","id":1377955,"title":"","content":"And so has my jaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T08:44:17-07:00","id":1377956,"title":"","content":"How did all of this broken plate get all over my floor...<br /> <br /> I'd best keep still until I have this figured out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:02:39-07:00","id":1377957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I feel like they really considered which aspects were weak in popular abilities (that make sense for a lot of characters).<br /> <br /> There's quite a few sorcerous initiations in there, if anyone missed it.<br /> <br /> And a 5pt merit where you get an Eclipse charm (and can potentially buy more) to represent being a God-Blood/Demon-Blood/etc.<br /> <br /> I haven't had time to read much of the fluff, but it was nice to see full write-ups of a number of Cadet Houses, which I think is very useful for some games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:14:47-07:00","id":1377960,"title":"","content":"So this isn't quite the full thing yet, but almost. It's the first six chapters, missing out on the new artifacts, the quick characters, and the Realm civil war/War in the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:24:02-07:00","id":1377963,"title":"","content":"I am still reading through it (I have just finished the Secondary Schools section)- but I must say that Stone Mask has just became my most favorite person in the Realm. It is all so awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:27:53-07:00","id":1377964,"title":"","content":"And now I feel stupid for not participating in the kickstarter...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:32:31-07:00","id":1377966,"title":"","content":"Holy mother of god they brought back As in the Beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:41:05-07:00","id":1377968,"title":"","content":"Can someone tell me about the material on the forest witches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:48:15-07:00","id":1377971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377966#post1377966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy mother of god they brought back As in the Beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they did. Yes they did...<br /> <br /> Made me think of the recent thread on here about Solars and area of effect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-02-2020, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:55:37-07:00","id":1377972,"title":"","content":"I am so fucking jealous of the backers now. I completely missed the kickstarter. I want to know and see what is in there so badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T09:59:07-07:00","id":1377975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377963#post1377963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still reading through it (I have just finished the Secondary Schools section)- but I must say that Stone Mask has just became my most favorite person in the Realm. It is all so awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is that? (Got work, so I will have to read it more later.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:11:59-07:00","id":1377978,"title":"","content":"They also added a lot more charms with teamwork affects. So many of the new ones are big game changers too, like enabling Elemental Bolt Attack to be used with Thrown or Archery charms, which lets me do something I\u2019ve wanted to for a while and use Persistent Hornet Attack with a hurled lightning bolt, or letting you block anima damage in an area and instead channel it into a decisive attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:26:15-07:00","id":1377984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377975#post1377975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is that? (Got work, so I will have to read it more later.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dominie of Pasiap's Stair. Very loyal to the students and the school. Extremely devoted to the Empress and her memory. Awfully disgusted but how the Empress's descendants act. Hope to gut at least one of the later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:26:40-07:00","id":1377985,"title":"","content":"Dragon's Egg Hatched is interesting. As a player, though, I doubt I would ever spend XP to learn this Charm when being a sorcerer with Summon Elemental is so much better.<br /> <br /> Granted, sorcery doesn't fit every character (and carries a stigma in the Realm that this Charm probably doesn't), but I haven't played many non-sorcerers with Occult 5 either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:32:00-07:00","id":1377989,"title":"","content":"Also, I'd like to point out World-Weaving Dragon Demiurge.<br /> <br /> This pretty well establishes that you <i>can</i>, in fact, have Charms that help with sorcerous workings. (Of course, that still leaves open the question of what a Solar or Lunar sorcerer might develop...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:41:24-07:00","id":1377992,"title":"","content":"I kickstarted but I didn't seem to get this, now I am sad. I guess I didn't fund up to a high enough level. Is there any cool new archery charms? I thought that tree needed some more pizzazz","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T10:47:42-07:00","id":1377995,"title":"","content":"There are a bunch of new archery charms, but I didn't read them closely. I'm sure someone else will go into them later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:17:12-07:00","id":1378001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377992#post1377992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kickstarted but I didn't seem to get this, now I am sad. I guess I didn't fund up to a high enough level. Is there any cool new archery charms? I thought that tree needed some more pizzazz</div> </div> </div> </div>How about one that lets you fire off ropes made of vines/smoke to reflexively move around the battlefield or pull objects towards you, one that lets you fire a landslide arrow that knocks enemies back and down, one that lets you turn your bow into a ballista, one to make an arrow bloom into a poisonous thicket, and one that lets you move while aiming?<br /> <br /> Also a charm in archery but applicable and purchasable by many abilities that lets you attune to a bunch of artifacts at once for cheap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:17:44-07:00","id":1378003,"title":"","content":"There are a LOT of Charms, these are just some of those that stood out to me :<br /> <br /> <b>Special</b> - Charm that reduces attunement cost of all artifact weapons after the first by 3, is simultaneously an <b>Archery</b>, <b>Brawl</b>, <b>Melee</b>, <b>Thrown</b> and <b>War</b> Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Archery</b> - Create a rope-arrow which also counts as a basic craft project! At E3, aim and move on the same turn for a small mote and ini cost. Also, you can turn your bow into a ballista and your flame weapon into a flame canon <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Athletics</b> - create ice under your feet, creating difficult terrain and allowing you to walk on water.<br /> <br /> <b>Awareness</b> - On join battle, transfer up to 5 ini to your allies (if they are hearthmates they get bonus ini). Also you can see the world as if you were at long range above your current position.<br /> <br /> <b>Brawl</b> - Cause an eruption, dealing aoe with lava.<br /> <br /> <b>Bureaucracy</b> - Once per Story, treat your Resources as 2 dots higher than they really are! Also easily convince someone that you are their superior or they should hire you in a position of authority.<br /> <br /> <b>Craft - </b>once per artifact you craft, if you gift it to a family member or hearthmate, unlock some of their evocations with white exp.<br /> <br /> the most powerful charm seems to be a <b>Dodge</b> Charm, I'm pretty sure it's actually OP right now in the right context. Reflexive counterattack after dodging which uses the <b>opponent's</b> initiative and benefits from <b>their</b> charms, to which you can then add <b>your own</b> Water Dragon Charms. If DBs have such a thing as a Solar killer Charm this is it. Also you get a Charm to catch arrows with your anima, that's pretty neat.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity</b> got amazing stuff. You can form a hearth/solar bond with a Lunar (!!!!!!!!!!). You can use your hearthmates' intimacies to resist influence!<br /> <br /> <b>Larceny</b> - has an incredibly evil Charm that helps you betray your hearthmates. Also a Charm to make your anima appear as a diffent aspect! <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Linguistics</b> - you can understand and be understood by all dragonbloods. you can &quot;steal&quot; a target's breath, causing them to speak quietly but granting you one language they know for the duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Melee</b> - too much awesome to list. Become a lightning rod that absorbs magical attacks, decisive with a lightning bolt, create a lava eruption <b>inside</b> your enemy, the works.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult </b>- bonuses on Sorcerous Workings which are elemental in nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Occult + Lore</b> - that's right, there is a dual ability charm. lets you keep some of your summoned elementals as familiars like a twilight.<br /> <br /> <b>Lore</b> lets you &quot;keep in&quot; your anima flux so you don't damage people and things around you, and then you can unleash it in a decisive to add damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Presence</b> lets you add half your appearance to your attack roll and then reduce your damage to improve the target's attitude towards you. If the attack would kill the target they fall unconscious instead but cannot spend willpower to resist your influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Sail</b> lets you treat your ship as solid ground for the purpose of Earth Charms which only work on solid ground. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Socialize</b> lets you take a bath to make everyone around you have a minor positive tie towards you for a week so long as you remain pleasant around them.<br /> <br /> <b>Survival</b> lets you convert uncountable environmental damage into 10 dice of damage and then roll Hardness to mitigate it.<br /> <br /> <b>War</b> lets you rally for numbers when you rout a battlegroup, recruiting from the enemy. Also you can join battle with war which doubles as a first turn free attack for your battle group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-02-2020, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:18:30-07:00","id":1378005,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the Outcasts section. The example outcasts in the end really show how even a lone outcast can make life for themselves as a demigod in faraway lands. The Cult of the Violet Fang competes with the Forest Witches for how strange they are- and that means something. I am only a bit disappointed that the Wanasaan didn't get some further expansion beyond the new Scions of Note, but those example characters did in fact expanded upon the coupe and its effect on the organization. Overall, I had some great fun reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:30:23-07:00","id":1378006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377968#post1377968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone tell me about the material on the forest witches?</div> </div> </div> </div>They get a full chapter, 20 plus pages. Think of an an extended Great House write-up from WFHW (plus a chapter fiction), with named noted figures and the like, plus rules for acting within the Sea of Mind (with starting character tweaks) and some style of play notes. Dead characters can even attune to walking effigies to interact with Creation. It's all suitably weird and looks kinda great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377992#post1377992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kickstarted but I didn't seem to get this, now I am sad. I guess I didn't fund up to a high enough level. Is there any cool new archery charms? I thought that tree needed some more pizzazz</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninja'd by others. There are six archery charms total though \u2013 that's amongst the most new charms, some abilities only got one I think.<br /> <br /> I personally really liked Dragon-Graced Raiment in resistance. Think Dragon-Graced Weapon but for your armour. Silent heavy armour \u2013 yes please.<br /> <br /> Imagine someone much more adept will do a 'reads' thread on it soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-02-2020, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:52:42-07:00","id":1378010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377968#post1377968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone tell me about the material on the forest witches?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are some of the most viscerally horrifying things I have ever read about, and I can't wait to use and/or play them.<br /> <br /> My inner Persona fan thanks the devs sincerely for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T11:55:31-07:00","id":1378012,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24647_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24647\" data-vbnamecard=\"24647\">Moss Reynholm</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:18:25-07:00","id":1378017,"title":"","content":"Divine Heritage is a simple and elegant Solution to a lot NPCs I have, and even PCs from previous games. Its a game changer tucked in this book not just for Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:22:34-07:00","id":1378026,"title":"","content":"Didn't get my charm changed like I asked, super disappointed. It's so fucking boring the way it was implemented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","name":"SunAndSpring","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12698_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:24:41-07:00","id":1378028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunAndSpring</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378026#post1378026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't get my charm changed like I asked, super disappointed. It's so fucking boring the way it was implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoot me an email or a DM on Discord and I'll get that done. Sorry I missed where you asked earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:28:34-07:00","id":1378032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divine Heritage is a simple and elegant Solution to a lot NPCs I have, and even PCs from previous games. Its a game changer tucked in this book not just for Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably the best way to do it, though I feel it may be slightly too open-ended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-02-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T13:31:23-07:00","id":1378035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1377985#post1377985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon's Egg Hatched is interesting. As a player, though, I doubt I would ever spend XP to learn this Charm when being a sorcerer with Summon Elemental is so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about &quot;so much better&quot;, actually. For one thing, Dragon's Egg Hatched is a Simple charm with no suggestion of requiring a dramatic action or anything to activate, meaning you can call up your elemental servant in a single turn in combat if you like, rather than the 4-hour ritual Summon Elemental requires. Also, the ST is the ultimate arbiter of what elementals exist in the setting, and is not under an obligation to allow an elemental perfectly customized to your needs, whether in powers or personality. The elemental summoned by Dragon's Egg Hatched, on the other hand, while probably less powerful than any elemental you could summon, is also more customized through the mutations you pick, and probably has fewer &quot;personality flaws&quot;, with only a single Major or Defining Intimacy chosen by the ST and based on its element, as opposed to the full suite of Intimacies a more standard summoned elemental would have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T14:53:33-07:00","id":1378052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378005#post1378005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoyed the Outcasts section. The example outcasts in the end really show how even a lone outcast can make life for themselves as a demigod in faraway lands. The Cult of the Violet Fang competes with the Forest Witches for how strange they are- and that means something. I am only a bit disappointed that the Wanasaan didn't get some further expansion beyond the new Scions of Note, but those example characters did in fact expanded upon the coupe and its effect on the organization. Overall, I had some great fun reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm showing my fanboyism here (which is a good problem to have in this case), but I got my next Lunar idea from there; a mortal Violet Fang who Exalted when he realized someone who was almost certainly a Forest Witch very far from home (guided by the numina and/or was a reincarnation who somehow got lost in Lethe and ended up in the body of a Guilder's kid) was sabotaging his sister's Pilgrimage and dived in headfirst to warn her. Luna caught him in the body of a Fair One who built up his self-confidence via mockery, and he joined her party in the form of a magpie as a guide away from the traps. Depending on where it's located, he's now advocating allowing some mortal pilgrims and expanding their lands, or followed the tides of Chaos back to where the saboteur came from.<br /> <br /> Because the Violet Fang is seriously cool. Also a good showing of how even the friendliest raksha are terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T15:28:48-07:00","id":1378060,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to have time for a thorough read until my first playthrough of Persona 5 Royal is done, but I'm skimming for the parts I'm particularly interested in and I absolutely love the section on secondary schools, especially the smaller ones. Great for a campaign setting and to help flesh out a character's backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T15:45:22-07:00","id":1378064,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can play Bolin now - you\u2019re welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:10:12-07:00","id":1378071,"title":"","content":"I did see lots of magma stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:14:10-07:00","id":1378073,"title":"","content":"Bleh.<br /> <br /> Feels kinda power-creep to me. Not unexpected when it comes to showing up the 'boring' Solars.<br /> <br /> Also not pleased that the DB get two fluff books and the Solars have gotten none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:36:12-07:00","id":1378084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378073#post1378073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleh.<br /> <br /> Feels kinda power-creep to me. Not unexpected when it comes to showing up the 'boring' Solars.<br /> <br /> Also not pleased that the DB get two fluff books and the Solars have gotten none.</div> </div> </div> </div>As In the Beginning is...kind of bonkers even for it's 1/year cooldown and super high cost. Everything else seems balanced with the corebook. Solars still totally dominate Dragonblooded, it's just that DBs got some more tricks like being able to use improvised weapons without the initiative cost, or able to treat a Lunar as their hearthmate. It does make them a bit more powerful, but in the way that every new MA released makes Solars more powerful, just by giving them options.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with you on the fluff though, but that's kind of situation of being a Solar. You emerge as the most powerful exalted, in a world where the Dragonblooded dominate world spanning empires and societies across Creation, and at the periphery Lunars have built their powerful domains over the past few thousand years. Solars are brand new on the block, they have no societies, no domains, no history except a legacy two ages past.<br /> <br /> We're probably going to get a lot of Lunar fluff in Many Faced Strangers detailing more of their domains and their elders as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:00:06-07:00","id":1378096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378073#post1378073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleh.<br /> <br /> Feels kinda power-creep to me. Not unexpected when it comes to showing up the 'boring' Solars.<br /> <br /> Also not pleased that the DB get two fluff books and the Solars have gotten none.</div> </div> </div> </div>DB mechanics in 3e limit their ability to spam or stack their most powerful effects keeping them well in check relative to Solars while still getting real potent fun effects unlike 2e\u2019s pathetic inability to even defend themselves. That principle applies just as much now as in What Fire Has Wrought, so I don\u2019t see how there\u2019s any \u201cpower creep\u201d.<br /> <br /> As for Solars not having \u201cfluff\u201d books... Solars don\u2019t have a uniting culture of any kind. So I don\u2019t know what a Solar \u201cfluff\u201d book would even be. They got a supplement that added big flashy Charms for them too. Arms of the Chosen heavily favored them over other Exalted. Eight Directions is next major supplement... what exactly are you looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-03-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:35:55-07:00","id":1378110,"title":"","content":"I guess you could do the Cult of the Illuminated? But I am kind of glad they haven't, because I think it should be much, much smaller than 1st ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:39:33-07:00","id":1378112,"title":"","content":"I'd also point out that there's a truly shocking amount of Dynastic Solars, so any DB fluff is Solar fluff... \ud83d\ude1c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:45:08-07:00","id":1378114,"title":"","content":"my charm turned out super awesome and at least one of my players is talking about how they want to take it so it worked out for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:50:18-07:00","id":1378116,"title":"","content":"Cult of the Illuminated is possible, but that might show up more in Gold Faction Sidereal fluff.<br /> <br /> Solars not having a lot of fluff is kind of a thing that helps to balance them out. Not like, to create parity so that mixed groups are all finely tuned and asymetrically balanced like Starcraft or anything. More just so that you either play a game where you're the greatest and most powerful heroes in the Exalted Host, or you're playing less than that, but with more support from the setting. Lunars have their schools, and domains, Sidereals have Heaven and the Bureau, and Terrestrials have their respective empires and immaculate faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:57:57-07:00","id":1378121,"title":"","content":"So, Tiger-and-Dragon Combination allows the two attackers to both use the higher of their Initiatives to deal damage.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I find distract gambits a lot more interesting. Not to mention Victory-Seeking Insight, that Awareness Charm that lets you donate Initiative to your teammates when you roll Join Battle.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit surprised that Magma Hell Upheaval doesn't get any special benefits against battle groups. I guess Dragon-Blooded just don't get army-killer Charms, unless you count As in the Beginning. (Speaking of which. If a battle group blows their rout check against AitB and dissolves, do they essentially become a bunch of trivial opponents who probably die in the blast? I mean, it's up to the ST whether trivial opponents just die in AitB or what, but I have to figure that a firestorm sweeping the earth for miles is at least as good at slaughtering fleeing dudes as a military unit chasing them would be.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:25:34-07:00","id":1378131,"title":"","content":"So can a Solar use God-King's Shrike to force some DB to use As in the Beginning at the appropriately timed moment, sucking away 30m, 3wp, and hitting them with a -4 penalty to everything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:31:58-07:00","id":1378133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378028#post1378028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shoot me an email or a DM on Discord and I'll get that done. Sorry I missed where you asked earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for getting back to me on my email so quickly! Hopefully we can get the charm worked out since as it is, it doesn't seem to be much different than lacing one's blade with, I dunno, mescaline, and one doesn't need to pay 8-10 xp to get mescaline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12698-sunandspring","name":"SunAndSpring","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12698_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:34:13-07:00","id":1378134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378131#post1378131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can a Solar use God-King's Shrike to force some DB to use As in the Beginning at the appropriately timed moment, sucking away 30m, 3wp, and hitting them with a -4 penalty to everything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think specifically. Like you couldn't activate the charm with the intent of forcing a DB to use As in the Beginning, but it's possible if you rolled between 2-4 successes that it might manifest that way. It's a lot more likely that that you'd trigger some kind of natural disaster with it.<br /> <br /> It's also just a really, really roundabout way to fight a Terrestrial. A Solar exalt can slay a terrestrial in a flash of golden light before the DB even has a chance to draw their weapon, it's a lot quicker and easier than using a 1/season charm and waiting a week.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:41:41-07:00","id":1378136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378131#post1378131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can a Solar use God-King's Shrike to force some DB to use As in the Beginning at the appropriately timed moment,</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in God-King's Shrike says that the Solar gets to pick the specific form the predicted disaster takes. In-universe, they're not <i>causing</i> the disaster at all, they're merely using their incredible grasp of Lore to predict a disaster that was going to happen. The ST is certainly free to say that, in certain cases, that disaster takes the form of a DB using As In The Beginning to blow everything up. But nothing says they have to do that, and if the ST wants a DB to be an antagonist, doing so seems silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:53:58-07:00","id":1378138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378121#post1378121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Tiger-and-Dragon Combination allows the two attackers to both use the higher of their Initiatives to deal damage.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, I find distract gambits a lot more interesting. Not to mention Victory-Seeking Insight, that Awareness Charm that lets you donate Initiative to your teammates when you roll Join Battle.<br /> <br /> I'm also a bit surprised that Magma Hell Upheaval doesn't get any special benefits against battle groups. I guess Dragon-Blooded just don't get army-killer Charms, unless you count As in the Beginning. (Speaking of which. If a battle group blows their rout check against AitB and dissolves, do they essentially become a bunch of trivial opponents who probably die in the blast? I mean, it's up to the ST whether trivial opponents just die in AitB or what, but I have to figure that a firestorm sweeping the earth for miles is at least as good at slaughtering fleeing dudes as a military unit chasing them would be.)</div> </div> </div> </div>While no, it does get an upgrade where it can be used with Ramparts of Obdient Earth so that is probably where you are gonna see it against Battle Groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T18:58:10-07:00","id":1378139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378116#post1378116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cult of the Illuminated is possible, but that might show up more in Gold Faction Sidereal fluff.<br /> <br /> Solars not having a lot of fluff is kind of a thing that helps to balance them out. Not like, to create parity so that mixed groups are all finely tuned and asymetrically balanced like Starcraft or anything. More just so that you either play a game where you're the greatest and most powerful heroes in the Exalted Host, or you're playing less than that, but with more support from the setting. Lunars have their schools, and domains, Sidereals have Heaven and the Bureau, and Terrestrials have their respective empires and immaculate faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. It also makes me curious on what kind of background support we will get from the new splats as well, Liminals and Getimians, with a lesser extent Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T21:17:30-07:00","id":1378177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378073#post1378073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also not pleased that the DB get two fluff books and the Solars have gotten none.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the splat that is explicitly the most numerous and diverse, plus largely ruling the roost for millennia, have a diverse and numbers-dependent set of cultures related to them compared to the guys who have literally been nonexistent for that long?<br /> <br /> Exalted 3E is moving away from &quot;the First Age is literally the predecessor to everything and everyone alive is just ruling the wreckage&quot; nonsense that drove much of 2E, and since this is a companion book to What Fire Has Wrought, it focused on societies with a lot of Terrestrial influence. The Realm book is also very stringently about the Realm first, not the Dragon-Blooded, so that really doesn't hold water as a critique; it's a mortals-in-DB-territory book.<br /> <br /> Besides, it kind of falls flat when a major mostly-antagonistic faction is, in fact, the long-term aftereffects of Solar dickery in the First Age, even if the origins are mostly a cautionary tale about treating people right these days (Forest Witches).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T21:19:28-07:00","id":1378178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378035#post1378035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about &quot;so much better&quot;, actually. For one thing, Dragon's Egg Hatched is a Simple charm with no suggestion of requiring a dramatic action or anything to activate, meaning you can call up your elemental servant in a single turn in combat if you like, rather than the 4-hour ritual Summon Elemental requires. Also, the ST is the ultimate arbiter of what elementals exist in the setting, and is not under an obligation to allow an elemental perfectly customized to your needs, whether in powers or personality. The elemental summoned by Dragon's Egg Hatched, on the other hand, while probably less powerful than any elemental you could summon, is also more customized through the mutations you pick, and probably has fewer &quot;personality flaws&quot;, with only a single Major or Defining Intimacy chosen by the ST and based on its element, as opposed to the full suite of Intimacies a more standard summoned elemental would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you can't summon an elemental perfectly customized to your needs, you can probably get something a lot closer to your needs than you'd get by spending 3-5 mutation points on what is otherwise pretty much an unintelligent mortal who can return to your side quickly but <i>can't</i> go more than a few miles away from you in the first place.<br /> <br /> It can't talk or follow complex commands, which excludes a lot of the major reasons I can think of for wanting a minor elemental in a hurry. And in retrospect, its inability to go far away from you is probably for the best, since it wouldn't be able to follow instructions well enough to be trusted that far from your supervision anyway.<br /> <br /> The personality issues of normal elementals are admittedly a thing, but I think the fact that (most) normal elementals can actually follow complex instructions balances that out.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Charm isn't useless. There are plenty of situations in which quickly whipping out an elite troop with increased soak (and no fear of dying in your service) might actually be helpful (especially if your group isn't especially optimized for combat). But I wouldn't spend the XP on it. I mean, it's a lot faster than sorcery, but sorcery lasts a lot longer, and the uses to which you can actually put these elementals are painfully limited.<br /> <br /> I might feel differently if DEH elementals were at least smart enough to use as scouts or something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T21:36:27-07:00","id":1378181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378073#post1378073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bleh.<br /> <br /> Feels kinda power-creep to me. Not unexpected when it comes to showing up the 'boring' Solars.<br /> <br /> Also not pleased that the DB get two fluff books and the Solars have gotten none.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both books describe locations solars can come from and institutions that they can interact with. The Realm and the first 4 chapters of Heirs are both Solar and Deeb fluff books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T22:40:35-07:00","id":1378188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378178#post1378178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the Charm isn't useless. There are plenty of situations in which quickly whipping out an elite troop with increased soak (and no fear of dying in your service) might actually be helpful (especially if your group isn't especially optimized for combat). But I wouldn't spend the XP on it. I mean, it's a lot faster than sorcery, but sorcery lasts a lot longer, and the uses to which you can actually put these elementals are painfully limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that Summon Demon/Elemental are just way too good at what they do. A lot of demons/elementals are highly specialized and powerful beings that sometimes even have special magical abilities that are very difficult to get otherwise. The biggest limiting factor is that if you abuse it too much you'll piss off the ST and/or other players, and that's no good.<br /> <br /> If DEH combines with Elemental Bond Meditation in that it lets you keep those summoned familiars indefinitely that might be something. Otherwise you're going to be taking the charm probably more for flavour than anything. Having two elemental bodyguards with enhanced senses watch over you while you sleep is okay, summoning a few venomous assassins to accompany you on a hunter killer mission is alright, making an impromtu mount with the centaur merit might be worth it if you're heavily invested in Ride, or just need to get somewhere at horse-speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:15:00-07:00","id":1378203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378188#post1378188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If DEH combines with Elemental Bond Meditation in that it lets you keep those summoned familiars indefinitely that might be something.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not. The elemental counts as a familiar if the DB also knows EBM (but does not count towards the maximum number allowed), but still dissolves at the end of the DEH's duration. However, the text allows that you can consider future summonings of the same element to effectively be the same character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-03-2020, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:44:39-07:00","id":1378209,"title":"","content":"Oh wait, this is just a portion of an unedited preview. That's all right then.<br /> <br /> I'm still not going to read it, I'm just unconcerned by that fact. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(Get back to Xenoblade Chronicles, you weakling)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm going, I'm going.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T02:19:03-07:00","id":1378216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378188#post1378188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the issue is that Summon Demon/Elemental are just way too good at what they do. A lot of demons/elementals are highly specialized and powerful beings that sometimes even have special magical abilities that are very difficult to get otherwise. The biggest limiting factor is that if you abuse it too much you'll piss off the ST and/or other players, and that's no good.<br /> <br /> If DEH combines with Elemental Bond Meditation in that it lets you keep those summoned familiars indefinitely that might be something. Otherwise you're going to be taking the charm probably more for flavour than anything. Having two elemental bodyguards with enhanced senses watch over you while you sleep is okay, summoning a few venomous assassins to accompany you on a hunter killer mission is alright, making an impromtu mount with the centaur merit might be worth it if you're heavily invested in Ride, or just need to get somewhere at horse-speed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378203#post1378203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does not. The elemental counts as a familiar if the DB also knows EBM (but does not count towards the maximum number allowed), but still dissolves at the end of the DEH's duration. However, the text allows that you can consider future summonings of the same element to effectively be the same character.</div> </div> </div> </div>DEH does seem one of the most characterful charms in there, but as pointed out above it's going to be really hard to balance given how much Occult 5 pushes you towards sorcery.<br /> <br /> (Also brings up a tendency I've noticed when I've been looking at building DBs: &quot;Hmmm, I really want Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique and Spirit-Grounding Shout because struggling to take on spirits hinders interacting with a lot of cool stuff in the game. I'm halfway to the four pre-req occult charms for sorcery already and ISoB as a control spell would be handy... and, aaargh, 75 per cent same as the last character. Start again...&quot;)<br /> <br /> (Not a complaint, more a lament about my min-maxing impulses).<br /> <br /> I'd maybe wanna make DEH Occult 3, Survival or Lore 3 to rein in the comparison to sorcery? Maybe the mutations and intelligence could get a slight bump too? The mutations people are most often going to apply I would guess are centaur (two dots - accessible at chargen as it stands, you always have access to a badass horse) and full wings (five dots) (although a wall-walking, gilled or venomous assassin would be fun too).<br /> <br /> Still, think it's so characterful I'd probably take it anyways even without any tweaks once I finally theory-craft something other than an Immaculate-trained sorcerer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-03-2020, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T05:41:35-07:00","id":1378239,"title":"","content":"Yo, I didn't notice this before now. I'll have reading for the night!<br /> <br /> I'm super happy with my backer charm, too. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel like I should mention that the idea for the Charm, Grasping Vine Shot, is courtesy of Sunder the Gold, so it's kind of his Charm as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-03-2020, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:30:22-07:00","id":1378303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378216#post1378216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd maybe wanna make DEH Occult 3, Survival or Lore 3 to rein in the comparison to sorcery? Maybe the mutations and intelligence could get a slight bump too? The mutations people are most often going to apply I would guess are centaur (two dots - accessible at chargen as it stands, you always have access to a badass horse) and full wings (five dots) (although a wall-walking, gilled or venomous assassin would be fun too).</div> </div> </div> </div>What if it was doubled up to (Essence x 2) mutation points instead? That way you could get an assassin with paralytic or blinding venom, or one with both enhanced vision and hearing or something. A centaur bodyguard with enhanced hide who always counts as being mounted for combat would be pretty good, plus at essence 4 you could trade the enhanced hide for full wings, and now you've got a flying centaur mount.<br /> <br /> You don't want to make it too good, the last thing Summon Elemental needs is the ability to do it as a simple action to call up a really powerful servant to do whatever you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T11:34:53-07:00","id":1378311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378303#post1378303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if it was doubled up to (Essence x 2) mutation points instead? That way you could get an assassin with paralytic or blinding venom, or one with both enhanced vision and hearing or something. A centaur bodyguard with enhanced hide who always counts as being mounted for combat would be pretty good, plus at essence 4 you could trade the enhanced hide for full wings, and now you've got a flying centaur mount.<br /> <br /> You don't want to make it too good, the last thing Summon Elemental needs is the ability to do it as a simple action to call up a really powerful servant to do whatever you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds cool. The flexibility of this seems more fun to play with than traditional summoning, IMO.<br /> <br /> Is anyone else bothered by Moon-and-Earth letting you use lunar bond charms? Wasn't the lunar bond supposed to reflect thousands of years of metaphysical buildup?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T12:21:38-07:00","id":1378316,"title":"","content":"I don't know. The bond came about after Lunars waged wars for several years against the supremacy of the Solars in the early First Age. The dragonblooded have been leading a powerful empire for over 700 years now and I could see something similar forming between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/439-plastic-doll","name":"Plastic Doll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:35:28-07:00","id":1378330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378303#post1378303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if it was doubled up to (Essence x 2) mutation points instead? That way you could get an assassin with paralytic or blinding venom, or one with both enhanced vision and hearing or something. A centaur bodyguard with enhanced hide who always counts as being mounted for combat would be pretty good, plus at essence 4 you could trade the enhanced hide for full wings, and now you've got a flying centaur mount.<br /> <br /> You don't want to make it too good, the last thing Summon Elemental needs is the ability to do it as a simple action to call up a really powerful servant to do whatever you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. I don't think it would seriously unbalance anything (the elementals not being intelligent is still a pretty sharp limiter on tasks for which they're useful), but it does open up the possibilities a bit more.<br /> <br /> Weird idea: what if the Charm only requires Occult 3 or 4, but you only get mutation points equal to twice your (lower of Essence and Occult)? I dunno, something just feels wrong to me about requiring Occult 5 here. Is this really a thing only grandmaster occultists should be able to do? (I dunno. I've often felt that Ability requirements on Charms go up faster than they really need to. But that issue is much bigger than this particular Charm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:10:43-07:00","id":1378345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378330#post1378330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a bad idea. I don't think it would seriously unbalance anything (the elementals not being intelligent is still a pretty sharp limiter on tasks for which they're useful), but it does open up the possibilities a bit more.<br /> <br /> Weird idea: what if the Charm only requires Occult 3 or 4, but you only get mutation points equal to twice your (lower of Essence and Occult)? I dunno, something just feels wrong to me about requiring Occult 5 here. Is this really a thing only grandmaster occultists should be able to do? (I dunno. I've often felt that Ability requirements on Charms go up faster than they really need to. But that issue is much bigger than this particular Charm.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably Occult 5 because even for Occult it's a pretty big stretch for a charm rather than a spell. If you were going to lower the Occult rating you might want to make it take more than a simple action, and make it more of a kind of ritual. As it is now plunging your hand into the ocean and pulling a water elemental into being at a whim is a pretty big deal fluff wise, even if it's not mechanically super powerful.<br /> <br /> In general though ability requirements go up too fast for my liking too, but I think that logic is probably why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:22:04-07:00","id":1378368,"title":"","content":"I mean, Occult 5 is where Solars get to create new spirits too.<br /> <br /> Granted, for Lunars it\u2019s Attribute 3, but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:10:06-07:00","id":1378393,"title":"","content":"Oh, so THAT\u2019S how the Empress can entrust warstriders to loyal DBs in an emergency, and they\u2019re able to wield their full power rather than not having Evocations yet to fight whatever the threat is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:27:49-07:00","id":1378397,"title":"","content":"As usual I got into the lore chapters and cared very little about the charms (not a mechanics guy and I cant tell whats overpowered or under-powered or useful to save my life, I just go with what seems cool).<br /> <br /> On the whole, I am happy with it aside from the utterly disgusting lack of warstriders (I am used to 3ed shanking me in the kidneys on this point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> My favorite point was the sharp dichotomy between societies.<br /> <br /> The Realm reeks of gender segregation, in the balance of notable characters as much as what they do. Basically a inverted medieval chronicle.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile you have the Lookshyians with a fairly egalitarian bend and a pretty even split between men and women.<br /> <br /> More tellingly is that you do not see many Imperator's having any official posts of power (and it seems like a tricky balance for those that do), the actual city command is held by members of their Gens to be sure but they do not cling to the positions themselves unlike the Realm. You don't get the sense that Karal Maiandreia is going to be able to make Linwei do anything with her Field Force that Linwei is not up for (or that the Field Force would go along with it) unlike the Realm where a Matriarch just has to snap her fingers and most any given general in her house will come running like an eager puppy.<br /> <br /> Its cool to see different societal ethos be highlighted.<br /> <br /> The lack of time on Gunzosha and other cool stuff makes me livid, but again I accept that is just 3rd being 3rd. And I am hopeful that we will see some attention paid to what life looks like for Gunzosha when we get the artifact blurb (and I am against all reason hoping that a high-tier backer asked for a mech or airship). Jokes aside though, the wordcount wasnt that enormous and the devs did great making use of the space they had to work with.<br /> <br /> I am curious as to what I see on this thread though, namely the 'dynast Solar' thing. Ive long heard it be said to be common and seen it at the table once, but I confess that it befuddles me. What do folks get out of a dynast Solar? I get Solar Wood Witches or Solar Lookshyians because there is more to them than 'because Dragon-Blooded are awesome' as a societal draw. Heck, even at worst you can get why the character would miss their life or think fondly back on it sometimes in play.<br /> <br /> You can only really get 'because I want my character to hate literally everything about their own background' out of a Celestial Dynast. That also sums up the attempts I have seen by the devs at Dynast Celestials. It kind of sounds like a miserable experience for both the player and the table to have a PC whose entire background is 'thanks, I hate it'. More so with 3rd falling like an avalanche to make sure that you cant possibly have anything remotely positive about it if you arent a DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 04-03-2020, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:50:18-07:00","id":1378399,"title":"","content":"For my take, Dyanst Solars have shown up enough times in my games I tend to ask folks nicely not to make them since I'm so god-damned bored wtih the trope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:17:37-07:00","id":1378404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378393#post1378393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so THAT\u2019S how the Empress can entrust warstriders to loyal DBs in an emergency, and they\u2019re able to wield their full power rather than not having Evocations yet to fight whatever the threat is!</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the Evocation awakening charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:30:26-07:00","id":1378409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378399#post1378399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my take, Dyanst Solars have shown up enough times in my games I tend to ask folks nicely not to make them since I'm so god-damned bored wtih the trope.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kDERlmd2NS4\" target=\"_blank\">We don't need another Lyta...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:30:52-07:00","id":1378410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378393#post1378393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so THAT\u2019S how the Empress can entrust warstriders to loyal DBs in an emergency, and they\u2019re able to wield their full power rather than not having Evocations yet to fight whatever the threat is!</div> </div> </div> </div>wait never mind, it only works with Artifacts you forged yourself. It wouldn\u2019t cover the Emoress entrusting First Age Warstriders to Dragon-Blooded champions when Lunar Kaiju attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:41:58-07:00","id":1378413,"title":"","content":"We haven't got the artefact chapter yet, (I was pleasantly surprised we got this at all), which is where I'd expect to find Gunzosha, airships and warstriders.<br /> So I don't quite get why people are upset why they aren't there yet.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm more concerned about the lack of guidelines for creating Eclipse charms, hopefully that will be covered in Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T17:52:09-07:00","id":1378418,"title":"","content":"I asked Vance on this and he said that he isn't sure that Exigents will have the room and that it might be better to do it when they do a book on Spirits. That said he did give me a good rule of thumb that should be useful with Exigent's charm creation advice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The basic rule of thumb is, they're things that don't compete directly with what Exalted Charms let you do, but instead open up some new weird capabilities</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:40:32-07:00","id":1378439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378397#post1378397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of time on Gunzosha and other cool stuff makes me livid, but again I accept that is just 3rd being 3rd. And I am hopeful that we will see some attention paid to what life looks like for Gunzosha when we get the artifact blurb (and I am against all reason hoping that a high-tier backer asked for a mech or airship). Jokes aside though, the wordcount wasnt that enormous and the devs did great making use of the space they had to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lookshy chapter fiction leaned pretty heavily into the first age artifact feel of some of Lookshy's stuff, although admittedly in its fallen age state without Solars to make new ones that's fading a bit. Sadly the DB kickstarter fell just short of adding new Warstriders to this companion, but I'm hoping I can use Gunzosha armor as a chasis for other like stuff.<br /> <br /> The idea that Cathak Meladus has an old cobbled back together but still servicable suit of Air Dragon power armor, or Lookshy's mostly mothballed fleet of first age airships and Sky Guard are really cool. Friggin, sky marines who I assume are like Lookshy's elite paratrooper division. Something that could be completely unexpected and take enemies totally off guard, and also an inspiration for Solar Twilight crafters as something they might be able to get back up and running fully, even if the infrastructure to make one from scratch simply doesn't exist anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just don't want it to creep back into the spotlight hogging that it kind of was becoming in later 2e. Like a magitech suit of power armor should be able to square off evenly against a 5-dot suit of artifact fullplate that's forged from the body of a precursor behemoth or something, and the real main power of the Realm's mighty navy should be its conventional forces. Just that once in a blue moon you might see one of it's first age battleships enter the arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T18:53:20-07:00","id":1378443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378409#post1378409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kDERlmd2NS4\" target=\"_blank\">We don't need another Lyta...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of the thing, why on earth is something like Lyta at all a desirable thing to play? Its sort of feels like I can hear 'crawling in my skiiiin' every time I hear someone start describing their idea for a Celestial Dynast. Exalted has always struck me as a really cool and feel-good game with depth, I don't understand the appeal of an archetype that is basically about making a character defined by 'my life sucks, everyone sucks, yay everything sucking'. It seems more like asking the entire table to suffer with you than anything fun to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378413#post1378413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't got the artefact chapter yet, (I was pleasantly surprised we got this at all), which is where I'd expect to find Gunzosha, airships and warstriders.<br /> So I don't quite get why people are upset why they aren't there yet.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm more concerned about the lack of guidelines for creating Eclipse charms, hopefully that will be covered in Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an incredibly unfair way of reading the complaint. <br /> <br /> Artifact descriptions up until now have been a quick history blurb followed by a metric wall of mechanics that eat most of its wordcount.<br /> <br /> More power to the folks that go for that.<br /> <br /> But I care about Gunzosha because of their unique place in the setting, I mean the <i>troopers</i> not the armor. I was hoping to hear about what they mean socially for Lookshy, how they impact their society and what the armor means to the wearer and how they relate to the world around them.<br /> <br /> An artifact blurb cant be that due in no small part to wordcount limits but also because it is describing the item. Trying to fit that into that small segment either robs the armors ability to be understood in other contexts or robs it of time that could be used to develop one of the things that makes Lookshy unique (although I have had more than enough discussions on this forum to know plenty of people want Lookshy to be down to 'Militarized Creation Society #452' or even 'I want the <i>benefits </i>of a Dynast, but don't want to have to read the Realm Lore'). <br /> <br /> Thats the rub for me, it pushes the Gunzosha to the side. It pushes them to this little corner where they can be neatly excised from the setting and that is one of the things that have been pushing me away from exalted. It feels increasingly like it is a game that has to fit to a very specific vision or you have to do so much work yourself that you might as well make another setting, thats not on the devs in full, frankly it has more to do with the hostility Ive been met with whenever I ask for more of a role for Magitech anywhere by the community. It makes a game that was at one point a very big part of my life feel like a battle to participate in.<br /> <br /> They did much the same with Warstriders, they have been marginalized to the point that the word has been used less than a dozen times outside of their arms chapter and one immediately gets passive-aggressive comments for asking for a bit more.<br /> <br /> Seeing Gunzosha pushed back to a word in the entirety of the Lookshy chapter in both books with the vague promise that I will get a whole entire blurb <i>does </i>feel like a kick in the teeth and one is immediately met with accusations of whining for not being jumping in joy for getting that much.<br /> <br /> For the record, I started and ended my comment by saying I loved the preview as a whole. But I honestly regret voicing my opinion because I immediately stirred a reaction that felt an awful lot like being called ungrateful for expressing the one thing I didnt like. I thought we were going for Exalted being more inclusive in ideas and concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T19:54:56-07:00","id":1378452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the record, I started and ended my comment by saying I loved the preview as a whole. But I honestly regret voicing my opinion because I immediately stirred a reaction that felt an awful lot like being called ungrateful for expressing the one thing I didnt like. I thought we were going for Exalted being more inclusive in ideas and concepts. </div> </div> </div>I hope you can find a good place in this community and I hope there's some cool description of Gunzosha life in the artifacts chapter for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats an incredibly unfair way of reading the complaint. </div> </div> </div>I think you may be reading a little too much into Fallen Eco's reply. When you complain about something, having someone misunderstand your complaint the first time is a pretty common experience, and &quot;I don't quite get why people are upset&quot; is a pretty mild rejoinder - it seems like someone who is very open to further explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T20:00:44-07:00","id":1378455,"title":"","content":"Well, the whole point about mortal gunzosha is that they're mortal. This is the companion book about Dragon-Blooded. They're not actually on-topic for the book. And they weren't included in the list of topics to be covered in this book (in the stretch goals in the Dargon-Blooded Kickstarter); the only direct mention of gunzosha was &quot;stats and Evocations for [Lookshy's] fabled gunzosha armor&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, well, gunzosha belong in a setting book for Lookshy equivalent to The Realm, not here, a book about the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I fully understand that can be frustrating, given that the pace of releases suggest that there won't be such a book, and the amount of information on Lookshy included here means it seems likely they won't be covered in Across the Eight Directions. Nevertheless, details on the place of gunzosha in Lookshy society don't really belong in a book focused on the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T20:07:11-07:00","id":1378456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378452#post1378452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you can find a good place in this community and I hope there's some cool description of Gunzosha life in the artifacts chapter for you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think you may be reading a little too much into Fallen Eco's reply. When you complain about something, having someone misunderstand your complaint the first time is a pretty common experience, and &quot;I don't quite get why people are upset&quot; is a pretty mild rejoinder - it seems like someone who is very open to further explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats fair and I do apologize for getting so heavy.<br /> <br /> Its just that as I said in the comment Ive felt increasingly marginalized as 3rd has proceeded. I am entirely too used to hostility and I have grown quick to react in kind.<br /> <br /> Honestly and embarassingly? Seeing that part hurt, weirdly and genuinely because I have been holding on to the hope of Heirs for a while. I tried my best to put on a good smile and voice my issue as light heartedly and unoffensively as possible. <br /> <br /> To see that even that was somehow an issue frankly made me snap a bit. As I said, Exalted has steadily felt like more of a battle than something pleasurable for me. It sounds silly I know, but frankly Ive just gotten to the point where it feels like I am being told to leave.<br /> <br /> Ive gotten used to grinning and bearing everyone dunk on the things that drew me into the setting (fantasy themes blended with technology, developed cultural clashes, an animesque blend of science and magic, etc). But it has gotten to the point where it is hard to maintain the pretense, especially when the one part I had deluded myself into thinking had survived is summarily brushed into a corner to make way for the only acceptable definition of diverse makes me depressed. <br /> <br /> Sorry again for going heavy, its just that its hard to articulate how I feel about this as well as I would like. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the kind word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:32:41-07:00","id":1378500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378345#post1378345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably Occult 5 because even for Occult it's a pretty big stretch for a charm rather than a spell. If you were going to lower the Occult rating you might want to make it take more than a simple action, and make it more of a kind of ritual. As it is now plunging your hand into the ocean and pulling a water elemental into being at a whim is a pretty big deal fluff wise, even if it's not mechanically super powerful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's also no limit on the number you can have active at once beyond (realistically) your willpower as far as I can tell. Be Prasasdi, max willpower, take Cult, make yourself a battlegroup of chameleon ninjas in minutes...<br /> <br /> It's a tough one to balance.<br /> <br /> I've wittered on about this one charm enough I suspect so I'm going to shove the rest of this behind a spoiler.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On my first reading, with zero justification, I definitely had this in my head as a creates one creature at time charm, sort of 'flow your anima into a substance and animate it', 'your daemon/personal anima come to life as a familiar' type aesthetic. (Also, weirdly, I've realised my default headcannon for elementals is nearly always animal-based, which is completely unjustified given my 2e experiences alone...)<br /> <br /> If the charm was one elemental at a time but still simple and offered DrLoveMonkey or Jefepato's ideas of more mutations I think dropping the Occult requirement and throwing in a minor Survival requirement would be okay, but otherwise, yeah, on reflection it's probably too massive a deal in terms of fluff alone to just be able to magic up so much so fast for it not to be top end Occult.<br /> <br /> I really like it as a charm though. Interested to see where it ends up.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-04-2020, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:43:32-07:00","id":1378501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378456#post1378456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted has steadily felt like more of a battle than something pleasurable for me. It sounds silly I know, but frankly Ive just gotten to the point where it feels like I am being told to leave.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a fondness for a lot of what you describe from 2e too (although am massively enthused by 3e). Hope you get what you're looking for out of the game soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:59:04-07:00","id":1378504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378456#post1378456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To see that even that was somehow an issue frankly made me snap a bit. As I said, Exalted has steadily felt like more of a battle than something pleasurable for me. It sounds silly I know, but frankly Ive just gotten to the point where it feels like I am being told to leave.<br /> <br /> Ive gotten used to grinning and bearing everyone dunk on the things that drew me into the setting (fantasy themes blended with technology, developed cultural clashes, an animesque blend of science and magic, etc). But it has gotten to the point where it is hard to maintain the pretense, especially when the one part I had deluded myself into thinking had survived is summarily brushed into a corner to make way for the only acceptable definition of diverse makes me depressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises glass*<br /> <br /> FWIW, I don't feel the aspects of the setting you like have gone away in fandom. It's just that after all this time the arguments have been had. Those who want that take on Creation don't gain anything by arguing with a fandom and creative team who have their own set vision in mind. So those elements of the fandom have largely just gone quiet, moved onto other games ect. We may still consider ourselves Exalted fans, we're just not so much a part of this community any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T05:37:41-07:00","id":1378507,"title":"","content":"Divine Heritage makes me happy, as do Heaven's Dragons and the Cult of the Violet Fang. Deadly Essence Flashpoint is neat for characters usually too far away to benefit from anima flux in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:30:12-07:00","id":1378518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378443#post1378443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of the thing, why on earth is something like Lyta at all a desirable thing to play? Its sort of feels like I can hear 'crawling in my skiiiin' every time I hear someone start describing their idea for a Celestial Dynast. Exalted has always struck me as a really cool and feel-good game with depth, I don't understand the appeal of an archetype that is basically about making a character defined by 'my life sucks, everyone sucks, yay everything sucking'. It seems more like asking the entire table to suffer with you than anything fun to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not everyone plays it the same way though. Black Company, Berserk and Elric are inspiration fictions. Numerous pulp heroic fiction exists around characters who aren't that likeable. Looking back at myth and saga, we see Achilles of the Iliad, Outlaws of the Marsh and so forth. And many more. Some people presumably will want to play a game where they play somewhat doomed, messed-up heroes, and presumably those some people will hopefully have scope at their table to all be on the same page with this and manage it.<br /> <br /> Sure, we can also play it as a more R-rated and adult version of your general JRPG / action-adventure / Saturday Morning Cartoon setup (and this is not in any way a slur, as I have some love for all those things) where all the characters are generally positive and likeable, with larger than life character and style and they generally like each other and get on and have no major personality problems (or at least no more than the relatively trivial disagreements we see in &quot;The Avengers&quot; and the like). That's fine too.<br /> <br /> You're only really going to get problems if you don't all agree on where you should be going. If someone's playing the doomed, troubled loner in your story about the fellowship and friendship of your circle.<br /> <br /> That said, even if no one is playing her, Lyta I see her reported as used quite a bit as an antagonist or foil. More so than many of the characters introduced by Caste Books. So there's some value in her from that, too.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Re; magitek again, I think we just tend to over-analyze this topic a bit. Really it's most summed up that they felt like they probably overshot both the fanbase's desire and what the core setting's feels supports for magitek, and dialing back a bit, for more focus on geomancy, sorcery, personal scale non-mechanical artefacts (magic rings, swords, etc). More &quot;Kingdom of Zeal&quot;, less &quot;Phantasy Star&quot; or &quot;FFXII&quot;, and certainly less &quot;modern day magic&quot;. You can still see some mechanistic stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:46:06-07:00","id":1378523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378397#post1378397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only really get 'because I want my character to hate literally everything about their own background' out of a Celestial Dynast. That also sums up the attempts I have seen by the devs at Dynast Celestials. It kind of sounds like a miserable experience for both the player and the table to have a PC whose entire background is 'thanks, I hate it'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not remotely my experience of it.<br /> Dynast Celestial is normally &quot;I want complex antagonist relationships with my relatives&quot;, the more mailigned version is when they want a free pass on the whole Anathema thing and to start out as something like Mnemon's secret asset who'll win her the civil war. Especially if they're trying to do it in what was intended to be a Dragon-Blooded game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T06:50:32-07:00","id":1378524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378523#post1378523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely my experience of it.<br /> Dynast Celestial is normally &amp;quot;I want complex antagonist relationships with my relatives&amp;quot;, the more mailigned version is when they want a free pass on the whole Anathema thing and to start out as something like Mnemon's secret asset who'll win her the civil war. Especially if they're trying to do it in what was intended to be a Dragon-Blooded game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I\u2019m going to be hunted, it might as well be intensely personal!<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a riches-to-rags-to-riches vibe, as well as an \u201cI can fix my broken homeland\u201d vibe, which are both appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T07:07:23-07:00","id":1378530,"title":"","content":"Broadly speaking, in my experience, there's 3 things going on: people want to play an aristocrat from a rich and powerful culture; people want to have family links with their enemy (one guy was the cousin of a member of the Wyld Hunt, another has a daughter who's a Dragonblood); and third, some people just really love the Dynastic background, so want a character from them (for example, one player really loved House Cathak, so she played a Zenith who'd grown up in House Cathak).<br /> <br /> Ironically, I don't think it's actually a <i>bad</i> concept, just overused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T08:56:22-07:00","id":1378552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378518#post1378518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re; magitek again, I think we just tend to over-analyze this topic a bit. Really it's most summed up that they felt like they probably overshot both the fanbase's desire and what the core setting's feels supports for magitek, and dialing back a bit, for more focus on geomancy, sorcery, personal scale non-mechanical artefacts (magic rings, swords, etc). More &amp;quot;Kingdom of Zeal&amp;quot;, less &amp;quot;Phantasy Star&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;FFXII&amp;quot;, and certainly less &amp;quot;modern day magic&amp;quot;. You can still see some mechanistic stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I am, too. People tend to forget just how damn hard it was to play someone who embraced being a sorcerer-engineer; for all of the setting focus, the rules really prevented you from enjoying being a techie. The greater focus on sorcery as a whole actually helped the feel, I think, because you don't need Exalted for sorcerers to do their thing.<br /> <br /> If anything, it actually fixed a major problem I had with 2E, the whole &quot;mortal exclusion&quot; thing. Nothing but circumstance prevents anyone from being a sorcerer, and Sorcerous Workings require less specialized skill than magitech. Now, not only do I have a plot hook for someone who thinks magic should be more accessible to all, but frankly, maintaining wonders of the First Age is a lot more plausible. So if anything, this makes Lookshy more capable of having magitech - there's more sorcerer-engineers to keep it going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:27:10-07:00","id":1378577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378345#post1378345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably Occult 5 because even for Occult it's a pretty big stretch for a charm rather than a spell. If you were going to lower the Occult rating you might want to make it take more than a simple action, and make it more of a kind of ritual. As it is now plunging your hand into the ocean and pulling a water elemental into being at a whim is a pretty big deal fluff wise, even if it's not mechanically super powerful.<br /> <br /> In general though ability requirements go up too fast for my liking too, but I think that logic is probably why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you're right. It's just that DEH in particular makes me think &quot;if I'm buying Occult 5 anyway, why not just play a sorcerer?&quot;<br /> <br /> Zany idea: what about an Essence 4-5 upgrade that allows the DB to whip out a (presumably small) battle group of elementals? If Summer Thunder's Evocations are any indication, it would probably cost something like 10m, 1wp, 3a.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if calling up an entire posse is beyond something a DB should be able to do. But high-Essence DBs aren't that common, anyway (and smaller battle groups aren't that scary). I kinda like the mental image of an elder DB stepping out of a burning building, snapping his fingers, and a squad of fiery warriors coalesce out of the blaze and fall into step with him.<br /> <br /> (Alternative idea: make it an Occult/War Charm that allows the DB commander to replace lost Magnitude in one of his subordinate units. Elementals rise up in the ranks to replace soldiers who have fallen or fled.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:35:37-07:00","id":1378578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378035#post1378035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about &quot;so much better&quot;, actually. For one thing, Dragon's Egg Hatched is a Simple charm with no suggestion of requiring a dramatic action or anything to activate, meaning you can call up your elemental servant in a single turn in combat if you like, rather than the 4-hour ritual Summon Elemental requires. Also, the ST is the ultimate arbiter of what elementals exist in the setting, and is not under an obligation to allow an elemental perfectly customized to your needs, whether in powers or personality. The elemental summoned by Dragon's Egg Hatched, on the other hand, while probably less powerful than any elemental you could summon, is also more customized through the mutations you pick, and probably has fewer &quot;personality flaws&quot;, with only a single Major or Defining Intimacy chosen by the ST and based on its element, as opposed to the full suite of Intimacies a more standard summoned elemental would have.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's the <i>Zero no Tsukaima / Familiar of Zero</i> Charm that Dragon-Blooded students of the Heptagram have been missing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T11:06:44-07:00","id":1378585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378239#post1378239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yo, I didn't notice this before now. I'll have reading for the night!<br /> <br /> I'm super happy with my backer charm, too. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Edit: I feel like I should mention that the idea for the Charm, Grasping Vine Shot, is courtesy of Sunder the Gold, so it's kind of his Charm as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Very cool, very useful, whether you're a forest elf Wood Aspect or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T11:15:05-07:00","id":1378588,"title":"","content":"Okay, so now Wood Aspect Link has a Hookshot, not bad, not bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T11:16:09-07:00","id":1378589,"title":"","content":"Pasiap Preempts Haste just threw me straight back to all of that work I did analyzing Clash Attacks together with smashing weapons, Earth Dragon Style, and Fist of the Titans.<br /> <br /> True, it's full power doesn't apply to clash attacks, but that's because its synergy with clash attacks is already very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T12:13:46-07:00","id":1378596,"title":"","content":"Hey, neat. Integrity's new Rot-Pruning Conviction is an effect I thought Dragon-Blooded might get as soon as we learned they could have any element under any Ability.<br /> <br /> It's a little odd, though. You can only use it to shed an Intimacy if you initially failed to resist the influence and needed to spend Willpower, but you can't use it to shed an unwanted Intimacy if you resisted successfully, even though that would be a greater statement of how ineffectual or undesirable the Intimacy is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T12:28:09-07:00","id":1378598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378596#post1378596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, neat. Integrity's new Rot-Pruning Conviction is an effect I thought Dragon-Blooded might get as soon as we learned they could have any element under any Ability.<br /> <br /> It's a little odd, though. You can only use it to shed an Intimacy if you initially failed to resist the influence and needed to spend Willpower, but you can't use it to shed an unwanted Intimacy if you resisted successfully, even though that would be a greater statement of how ineffectual or undesirable the Intimacy is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have access the Charm so maybe I'm missing something obvious, but... why would you need to shed an unwanted Intimacy if you resisted the influence to instill it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T12:42:31-07:00","id":1378601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378598#post1378598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have access the Charm so maybe I'm missing something obvious, but... why would you need to shed an unwanted Intimacy if you resisted the influence to instill it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't shed one on instills, you do so on a persuade or similar roll to make you do something. It's after you spend willpower to resist.<br /> <br /> And I agree that needing to fail to resist first is unusual, but it's quite powerful, letting you discard an intimacy you no longer desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:01:31-07:00","id":1378602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378601#post1378601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't shed one on instills, you do so on a persuade or similar roll to make you do something. It's after you spend willpower to resist.<br /> <br /> And I agree that needing to fail to resist first is unusual, but it's quite powerful, letting you discard an intimacy you no longer desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite powerful, especially because it lets you evict an Intimacy that ALMOST got you to do something you didn't want to do, instead of an Intimacy that enabled a failed attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:06:49-07:00","id":1378605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378588#post1378588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so now Wood Aspect Link has a Hookshot, not bad, not bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite a Hook Shot, but close. And it's a form of Hook Shot he can use without needing to put his bow away.<br /> <br /> <br /> These Charms are all really cool. Wood-Devil's Mask can now be used to make artifact masks, Tiger-and-Dragon Combination finally gives us <i>Chrono Trigger</i> Dual Techs without Crimson Pentacle Blade Style, a Dragon-Blood can become a Lunar's Terrestrial Mate, crafters can gift artifacts to others and unlock Evocations for them... Just too many things to mention, and I'm not even done.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can perform something like that one trick Kakashi used against Sasuke during the bell test, except Kakashi only buried Sasuke up to his chin and then left him there without further grappling with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T16:12:46-07:00","id":1378626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378397#post1378397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole, I am happy with it aside from the utterly disgusting lack of warstriders (I am used to 3ed shanking me in the kidneys on this point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall right, that was the last stretch goal we didn't quite get funded. Its a tragedy is what it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T17:52:01-07:00","id":1378641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378456#post1378456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats fair and I do apologize for getting so heavy.<br /> *SNIP*</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise for upsetting you, it was not my intent.<br /> <br /> Thank you for explaining WHY it mattered to you. I'm sorry that Heirs disappointed you in that way. I hope you can still enjoy the product (and third edition, preferably without slogging it out).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T11:30:32-07:00","id":1379026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1378523#post1378523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not remotely my experience of it.<br /> Dynast Celestial is normally &quot;I want complex antagonist relationships with my relatives&quot;, the more mailigned version is when they want a free pass on the whole Anathema thing and to start out as something like Mnemon's secret asset who'll win her the civil war. Especially if they're trying to do it in what was intended to be a Dragon-Blooded game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets complex when the storyteller section of the 2e Dragon Blooded book encourages this as a mode of mixed splat play. :|","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":5526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","user":"Steamfunk","date":". 04-07-2020, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:34:45-07:00","id":1379049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379026#post1379026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This gets complaex when the storyteller section of the 2e Dragon Blooded book encourages this as a mode of mixed splat play. :|</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird in that it throws shade on wanting to play a Celestial in a Dragon-Blooded game (or maybe in general? it can be read as such) but nevertheless attempts to support that game format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-06-2020, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:53:35-07:00","id":1379064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379049#post1379049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird in that it throws shade on wanting to play a Celestial in a Dragon-Blooded game (or maybe in general? it can be read as such) but nevertheless attempts to support that game format.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chargen section threw shade at wanting to play a Celestial at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP Dragon-Blooded</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players of Dragon-Blooded have an advantage where roleplaying is concerned. If you're playing a Terrestrial Exalt rather than, say, a Solar or Abyssal character, odds are that power gaming isn't your cup of tea anyway, so you're free to come up with a character who really interests you - a character with depth, complexity, and shortcomings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't do it often these days, but that definitely warrants a return to ha ha ha oh wow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:09:06-07:00","id":1379198,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I sofened my approach in light of the person at the start of this conversation chain saying that they felt increasingly marginalised for enjoying the 2e tone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:42:13-07:00","id":1379210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379064#post1379064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't do it often these days, but that definitely warrants a return to ha ha ha oh wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading that uncharitably.<br /> <br /> It's not saying &quot;if you are playing a Solar then you are powergaming -- interesting Solars with weaknesses are not allowed&quot;. <br /> <br /> It's saying &quot;if you are willing to deliberately nerf your character to all hell (by playing a Dragon-Blooded) then you may as well lean into the fact that you are weaker to create a character that interests you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which, I think, is right.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a min-maxed DB trying to compete 1-on-1 with Solars then you are doing it wrong*. Just play a Solar, pal. If you want to play a weaker character because they are weaker then play a weaker character. <br /> <br /> It all comes back to Session 0 expectations of the game.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against Dynast Solars (I don't think I've ever played one). I have nothing against 2E magitech (it's my favourite part of 2E, but I enjoy 3E's aesthetic now I've given it a chance).<br /> <br /> I've played a lot of mixed games. Frankly 3E is the best support I've seen for that. I &quot;get&quot; the complaint, but it comes down to what the players want and expect. The same playstyles and ideas won't be fun for everyone.<br /> <br /> *In my opinion. If you're using my own power-gamer builds in a mixed Exalt game and everyone is having fun as your T-Rex riding Dynast creates volcanoes in her wake then play on! You do what works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T10:10:39-07:00","id":1379266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379210#post1379210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're reading that uncharitably.<br /> <br /> It's not saying &quot;if you are playing a Solar then you are powergaming -- interesting Solars with weaknesses are not allowed&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's saying &quot;if you are willing to deliberately nerf your character to all hell (by playing a Dragon-Blooded) then you may as well lean into the fact that you are weaker to create a character that interests you&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st off, if it was the case, it was really badly worded. 2nd off, the rest of the chapter is extremely preachy about this sort of thing in a way that Exalted usually isn't, and for good reason. It tends to assume that you're playing a powerful character, objections of old hands from the WoD be damned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which, I think, is right.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a min-maxed DB trying to compete 1-on-1 with Solars then you are doing it wrong*. Just play a Solar, pal. If you want to play a weaker character because they are weaker then play a weaker character. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's correct. There's nothing that says that Dragon-Blooded can't be optimized due to character traits. They'll also likely end up sidelined at the Office of Harmony, because that type probably ended up the victim of &quot;unfortunate accidents&quot; more often than usual in the name of political expedience. The game even richly rewarded Dragon-Blooded for getting triple-specialized in something, because that was the die cap for their Charms, which was half as costly as for Celestials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It all comes back to Session 0 expectations of the game.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against Dynast Solars (I don't think I've ever played one). I have nothing against 2E magitech (it's my favourite part of 2E, but I enjoy 3E's aesthetic now I've given it a chance). </div> </div> </div>I thought the convo had mutated into being about weird writing tone. The above had nothing to do with Dynast Celestials; it was Celestials in general. The Storytelling chapter of each manual had a section where it addressed multiple Exalted games, and it mentioned that Dragon-Blooded were weaker, but could still work to take down the same threats that Solars did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T10:50:56-07:00","id":1379274,"title":"","content":"I think there is a subset of people who want to play at a solar power tier but have trouble coming up with an engaging concept for one. These same people may like the aesthetics and themes of dragon blooded but are put off by their lower power tier. <br /> <br /> So I can see why one might find themselves attempting to powergame a dragon blooded and wishing they were stronger in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:19:23-07:00","id":1379296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379266#post1379266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's correct. There's nothing that says that Dragon-Blooded can't be optimized due to character traits. They'll also likely end up sidelined at the Office of Harmony, because that type probably ended up the victim of &quot;unfortunate accidents&quot; more often than usual in the name of political expedience. The game even richly rewarded Dragon-Blooded for getting triple-specialized in something, because that was the die cap for their Charms, which was half as costly as for Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're just a pure powergamer you can't be a DB, you also need to be a sorcerer, it's too low investment for too much return. Can't use thrown, it's really good in some places, but melee is just better in more areas and is therefore the only option you can take. You can't take merits like Backing or Allies, partially because they're unreliable and could possibly even be used against you to make you do things, and partly because you don't have dots left over after the artifacts, hearthstones, quick reflexes, etc.<br /> <br /> If you're playing in a DB game though you're clearly not that concerned with being the greatest, most busted combo invincible character ever. Especially in 2e the greatest, most optimized DB still falls totally flat against even a marginally powerful Solar. Since your sole motivation isn't to make a character who can never lose, why not start with an interesting character concept first and then build around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379274#post1379274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a subset of people who want to play at a solar power tier but have trouble coming up with an engaging concept for one. These same people may like the aesthetics and themes of dragon blooded but are put off by their lower power tier.<br /> <br /> So I can see why one might find themselves attempting to powergame a dragon blooded and wishing they were stronger in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine there are some people like that, but I don't understand it at all. Solars are the exalt type with the absolute least baggage attached to them, basically nothing except that they're treated as horrible monsters and hunted by the Wyld Hunt. They should, and are designed to, fit basically any character concept you can think of, except maybe ones that hinge hard on being a weak little cog in a grand machine or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:44:43-07:00","id":1379301,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but that same blank slate that allows them to fit basically any character concept also leaves them prone to blandness if you don't know what you're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:12:18-07:00","id":1379309,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I suspect one reason for how common &quot;Solar Dynast&quot; as a concept is that it comes with a lot of background. Compared to making a really interesting Solar, making an interesting Dragonblood is relatively simple; pick one of 11 houses (or Outcast), pick one of 5 Aspects, pick one of 4 secondary schools. You've already got a pretty detailed background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:07:47-07:00","id":1379319,"title":"","content":"I'd tend to guess the Solar default situation as kind of wandering heroes, tends to optimize more for characters who become interesting through play by exploring how they show their character (and how their character is tested and changed) by a variety of situations, and as they form relationships with each other and with people they meet. <br /> <br /> Think of your traditional lone or small group wandering hero / &quot;fish out of water&quot; story (pretty arguably the absolute vast majority of fantasy fiction and fantasy adjacent heroic / sci-fi fiction, movies, etc), that when those characters became most interesting was often when their true character was revealed and tested by becoming enmeshed in events.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded Dynasts are great for exploring complexity and character in often conflicting and emotionally ambiguous relationships full of political and social complexity, from the start. (I'm reading Wolf Hall right now, which is a pretty engaging novel that you could perhaps classify as being within the genre of historical intrigue fiction, and hence some of my thoughts on this topic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:16:48-07:00","id":1379325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379301#post1379301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that same blank slate that allows them to fit basically any character concept also leaves them prone to blandness if you don't know what you're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I've heard, but I've been playing this game since the start of 2e and I have encountered maybe 4 people who I would describe as &quot;knowing what they are doing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:47:50-07:00","id":1379342,"title":"","content":"So, er, what happened to Nissar? His cadet house was formed just a century ago, so you'd expect him to still be around, or at least <i>recently</i> dead, but the text doesn't spare a word for him after the initial paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T16:25:21-07:00","id":1379350,"title":"","content":"I'm mean, given how Wu-Jian was described. He probably died quite the time ago with a knife in his back.<br /> <br /> Note that while Exalts can have long lives, most don't. And with Nissar I'd say it was definitely how it went down","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T17:12:40-07:00","id":1379355,"title":"","content":"Yep. I agree that the house tradition, of scions struggling with whether they should conspire against their elders or betray such conspiracy to curry favours, likely had an early start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:24:23-07:00","id":1380128,"title":"","content":"What level of backer was/is needed to get access to the preview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:45:06-07:00","id":1380136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1380128#post1380128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of backer was/is needed to get access to the preview?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not official and don't know for sure. However, I would <i>guess</i> that anyone whose pledge included Heirs to the Shogunate would get the preview. Looking over the Kickstarter campaign page, that appears to be the $40 pledges and up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:49:42-07:00","id":1380149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1379301#post1379301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that same blank slate that allows them to fit basically any character concept also leaves them prone to blandness if you don't know what you're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don\u2019t see that. Solars are humanity writ epic-scale. They\u2019re as interesting as any given epic hero character concept. If by \u201cknow what you\u2019re doing\u201d you mean \u201chave a character concept\u201d... yeah Solars are only as interesting as their individual character concepts, that\u2019s true - and the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:32:15-07:00","id":1380233,"title":"","content":"So, fun fact (which maybe some of you knew, but I didn't); Wanassen is an ancient Mycenaean word meaning &quot;Queens&quot;. In Mycenaean religion, it sometimes talks about two &quot;<i>Wanassen</i>&quot;, and it's believed this is referring to Demeter and Persephone... Persephone, of course, is alive yet rules the Underworld as its queen.<br /> <br /> So a very appropriate word for Dragonblood who traffic with, command, and banish ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:03:35-07:00","id":1380762,"title":"","content":"Are there canonical elements for the Cadet Houses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:10:56-07:00","id":1380765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1380762#post1380762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there canonical elements for the Cadet Houses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you counting the Prasadi clans as Cadet Houses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:15:22-07:00","id":1380766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1380762#post1380762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there canonical elements for the Cadet Houses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ferem is Air, Nissar is Water, Yueh is implied to be Water, and Simendor is sorcery-focused, implying Air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:50:19-07:00","id":1380774,"title":"","content":"What implies Yueh is Water other than being in the West?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reacti