"id":1380783,"title":"","content":"I could see those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T00:04:58-07:00","id":1380878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1380774#post1380774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What implies Yueh is Water other than being in the West?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're described as a family of mariners, warriors and merchants; that points in the direction of the Water Aspect abilities, but they could be more in a V'neef situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T01:40:12-07:00","id":1380883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1380762#post1380762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there canonical elements for the Cadet Houses?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine the Cadet houses don't actually have enough DBs to have a dominant Element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T03:16:45-07:00","id":1380893,"title":"","content":"Any early favourites for people amongst the Cadet Houses?<br /> <br /> The chapter fiction made me wonder about Nissar and Peleps' relationship. I guess the candidate would be Aramida, although my head canon for them always centres on a western expansion rather than a bid for the Realm itself.<br /> <br /> I could see Peleps using some Nissar skulduggery, either as catspaws or as sacrificial lambs (I.e. they expose them) as an excuse to 'intervene for the sake of peace' in the west and carve out the new empire.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also very curious to see Devil Pipe style...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-13-2020, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T17:51:28-07:00","id":1381479,"title":"","content":"Everyone check your backerkit<br /> <br /> Part 2 has dropped","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:05:39-07:00","id":1381502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381479#post1381479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone check your backerkit<br /> <br /> Part 2 has dropped</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so glad my exam just finished rather than having to skip studying if it dropped last night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:27:37-07:00","id":1381507,"title":"","content":"Gunzosha armor is definitely just the kind of thing I was looking for as a basis for Dragon Armor. It might even be worth not even making the distinction. Dragon Armor is just the 4-N/A dot Gunzosha armor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:38:36-07:00","id":1381508,"title":"","content":"Holy shit I love Fivefold Dragons' Grasp.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a bit bizarre, and honestly Ascendant Omphalos Avatar seems like a serious pain to actually use, but it's got a cool theme and it did something genuinely interesting with the DB Aura mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:41:19-07:00","id":1381509,"title":"","content":"You could have dragon armour be a subset of gunzosha with additional standardized evocations geared towards dragon blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:44:32-07:00","id":1381510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381509#post1381509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have dragon armour be a subset of gunzosha with additional standardized evocations geared towards dragon blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T20:15:30-07:00","id":1381514,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, if dragon armour retains its ability to be used by mortals, it makes passing it down a family much easier. No dragon blooded heirs? No problem!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T21:17:54-07:00","id":1381521,"title":"","content":"Here's a quick run-down of the Artifacts :<br /> <br /> <b>1) The Dragon-Dancer\u2019s Wings (Blue and Red Jade Typhoon Fangs, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Fire and Ice War Fans that allows dancers to rouse the depressed or becalm those taken by rage. Its capstone cures Psyche effects and can lower Derangements for a whole Story.<br /> <br /> <b>2) Empyrean Aegis (Blue Jade Thunderbolt Shield, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Ice Shield which the user can throw at enemies ala Captain America. Its main function is to be thrown in the path of attacks to protect allies. The capstone lets you Defend Other a whole group of allies from range.<br /> <br /> <b>3) Majestic Nightmare Visage (Green Jade Devil Mask, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A Mask that lets you take on the persona of a mythic fae lord schemer and plotter. The mask's power are especially effective against fae. The capstone grants a reservoir of points to be spent in schemes, similar to the Solar Larceny Charm Master Plan Meditation.<br /> <br /> <b>4) Sunset Blaze (Red Jade Direlance, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A flaming spear for an army general, it rallies troops and hunts down enemy generals. The capstone can empower all allied battle groups with many benefits, including +1 Size and Perfect morale, and it can be used every battle.<br /> <br /> <b>5) White Lizard\u2019s Tongue (White Jade Direlash, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> An Earth Whip for the Exalted herd wrangler in you! Brands allies and cattle to protect them or brand foes to weaken them. The capstone triggers a large earthquake that deals damage and sends enemies prone.<br /> <br /> <b>6A) Windblades (Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Windblades are a category of First Age Artifact, a disc-shaped Heavy Thrown Weapon which can be ridden as a flying platform and shrunk down when not in use.<br /> <br /> <b>6B) Blazerider (Red Jade Windblade, Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Blazerider is a flame themed Windblade which heavily specializes in aerial combat. It can be used as a weapon even while you are flying it! Its capstone creates a massive flame tornado.<br /> <br /> <b>7) Conquering Tide (Black Jade Warship, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A ship for policing the seas and enforcing justice, it helps investigation and hinders manipulation. Its capstone forces a criminal to atone for their crimes by subjecting them to a geas proportional to the gravity of their crimes.<br /> <br /> <b>8) Fivefold Dragons\u2019 Grasp (Green Jade Smashfist, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Elemental gloves that greatly enhance Elemental Bolt and greatly loosen the restrictions on Auras. The capstone allows the wielder to fully ignore the bonfire Aura restrictions and it allows you to count as being in multiple Auras at the same time<br /> <br /> <b>9) Glacial Mantle (Blue Jade Articulated Plate, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A frozen armor for a general, it manipulates ice, creates environmental hazards and enhances battle groups. The capstone can grant battlegroups many benefits, including Might 2 and Overwhelming 5, and can be used every battle. A General wielding both this and Sunset Blaze is probably an absolute terror.<br /> <br /> <b>10) The Revelation Sphere (Blue Jade Puzzle, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A utility artifact for sorcerer-scholars, it helps the wielder track down ancient places of power and shape sorceries, especially investigative sorcery. The capstone enhances spellcasting in various ways for a Scene, including the possibility of reducing the willpower cost of spells by 1.<br /> <br /> <b>11A) Gunzosha Armor (Artifact \u00a7 \u2022\u2022\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Gunzosha Armor is a category of First Age Heavy Artifact armor. It can be used by mortals, but only if they undertake a surgery that halves their lifespan. All Gunzosha Armor shares a base set of Evocation reflecting the advantage of fighting in a Power Armor, however each armor also unlocks its own set of Evocation based on its own legend.<br /> <br /> <b>11B) Seralawi, the Earth\u2019s Beating Heart (White Jade Gunzosha Armor, Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A defensive Gunzosha Armor whose 3 Evocations are all E1 and all have an alternate cost of 1wp instead of motes, so they can all be used by mortals. It focuses on Soaking hits and granting benefits when the wielder successfully soaks hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-15-2020, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T21:26:56-07:00","id":1381522,"title":"","content":"I'm really surprised to see the suggestion than an Incarna might become involved in the Realm civil war. I'm trying to imagine what that would even look like, and why. Maybe Serenity can't stand the thought of a global conflict erupting? Or maybe Conky takes a liking to one person in particular and gives them divine support?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T21:35:14-07:00","id":1381523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381522#post1381522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really surprised to see the suggestion than an Incarna might become involved in the Realm civil war. I'm trying to imagine what that would even look like, and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't surprise me, but then again, just what you've said immediately brings the <i>Iliad</i> to my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T21:37:53-07:00","id":1381524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381523#post1381523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't surprise me, but then again, just what you've said immediately brings the <i>Iliad</i> to my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, I can see that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T22:38:36-07:00","id":1381531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381508#post1381508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit I love Fivefold Dragons' Grasp.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a bit bizarre, and honestly Ascendant Omphalos Avatar seems like a serious pain to actually use, but it's got a cool theme and it did something genuinely interesting with the DB Aura mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one is the one I backed. I wanted to have something akin to an Essence lens from previous editions that also messed around with the Wu Xing idea they wanted to do with DBs originally but couldn't. I'm really happy how it came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T23:06:54-07:00","id":1381536,"title":"","content":"For those thirsty for the Void, there's a bit in the Realm Civil War about how the Silver Prince sees the world.<br /> <br /> Thankfully for everyone, especially the fans, most of his cynicism has been jettisoned to leave the much more interesting social scientist-turned-pirate king behind. He genuinely believes in ennoblement through undeath, and he wants to turn all of Creation into a perfect society - his victory is inevitable, he feels, because Skullstone is just a better place to live in, and eventually the living will see that. His mindless undead help keep Skullstone free of the Guild and Azure's slavers, and should the War in the West erupt, he has no intention of conquering the Realm; he's a deathlord, he can wait for their descendants to come to him. Really, he's going to be helping with keeping the neutral powers out of the fray in return for some new shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T23:36:29-07:00","id":1381541,"title":"","content":"He's going for the Cultural Victory route I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:32:52-07:00","id":1381547,"title":"","content":"What's this you say? No mysterious second-age Doom Fleet lurking in the shadows? No overly-convoluted &quot;second coming&quot; plot?<br /> <br /> Yes! We got a peek at this openly-ruling true-believer Silver Prince in the core book, and Heirs expands on these details nicely.<br /> <br /> It makes Skullstone a much more interesting landmark to navigate--geographically and politically--.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:48:09-07:00","id":1381553,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really glad to see how all the powers in the West are portrayed. Even the weaker ones are portrayed as actors that need to be taken very seriously, and the stronger ones aren\u2019t portrayed as unchallengeably overwhelming. Even with the Abyssals Skullstone is no match for the Water Fleet, but they have a mysterious and undeniable power that either needs to be dealt with, or can be used to advantage, or TAKE advantage of the situation, and will almost certainly end up a combination of all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:51:16-07:00","id":1381555,"title":"","content":"This is probably a brain fart and the answer is obvious so I\u2019m asking here before I bug Vance on the Dev thread. For an Exalted wearing Gunzosha Armor, would the extra dice from Integrated Essence Musculature on a Strength based roll count toward their Charm dice cap? I\u2019m assuming yes, but I wanted to double check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:06:05-07:00","id":1381558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1381555#post1381555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a brain fart and the answer is obvious so I\u2019m asking here before I bug Vance on the Dev thread. For an Exalted wearing Gunzosha Armor, would the extra dice from Integrated Essence Musculature on a Strength based roll count toward their Charm dice cap? I\u2019m assuming yes, but I wanted to double check.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, too, <i>but</i> it might be worth checking the intention since mortals <i>do not even have a dice adder cap</i>. <br /> <br /> While at it, perhaps also asks how this interacts with charms like Strength of Stone Technique.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T01:33:23-07:00","id":1381562,"title":"","content":"Oh boo, for some reason I thought Dazan was one of the characters we were getting a QC writeup for. At least my table canon that he\u2019s Wood Aspect is intact. Oh, as is my own portrayal of the identity of V\u2019neef\u2019s father (a Prasadi emissary, she and Oban [who is her full brother] would look Desi in the context of our world\u2019s racial constructs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-15-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:07:42-07:00","id":1381622,"title":"","content":"edit: NM, didn't check in yesterday and only got the email this morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:14:00-07:00","id":1381623,"title":"","content":"QC discussion below, now spoiler