,"date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T02:31:10-07:00","id":1382088,"title":"","content":"We don\u2019t have an identity on the Admiral of the Merchant fleet, do we?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s a V\u2019neef, though probably (given the very high rank and responsibility, and the age of the House) an adopted one? Presumably a former Found Egg who the Empress would have personally trusted to oversee her tributes, before they were adopted as a V\u2019neef?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-17-2020, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T03:15:46-07:00","id":1382102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382078#post1382078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given everything else Ragara has gotten up to and the way the timeline sets that up, I honestly find that very suspicious. It would not surprise me one bit to discover that Ragara framed them up and down in order to get his own house. Or that he was behind them getting Eyem. Or that Eyem is now in HIS basement giving him solid financial advice, because he cooked the books so everyone would think it was an evil mastermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's Ragara specifically.<br /> A lot of the Great Houses struck from the Imperial Registry were conspiring against the Empress because she was already carving up their assets and looking for the first sign of resistance to go &quot;Oh, now I can say I was provoked.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T04:30:30-07:00","id":1382117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382078#post1382078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given everything else Ragara has gotten up to and the way the timeline sets that up, I honestly find that very suspicious. It would not surprise me one bit to discover that Ragara framed them up and down in order to get his own house. Or that he was behind them getting Eyem. Or that Eyem is now in HIS basement giving him solid financial advice, because he cooked the books so everyone would think it was an evil mastermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it seems most likely it was an evil mastermind... And also it's in his basement giving financial advice! \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> Anyway, in the high-pressure society of 10,000 Exalted nobles, it hardly seems surprising that some Houses really do plot to overthrow their ruler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T04:31:41-07:00","id":1382118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382088#post1382088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don\u2019t have an identity on the Admiral of the Merchant fleet, do we?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s a V\u2019neef, though probably (given the very high rank and responsibility, and the age of the House) an adopted one? Presumably a former Found Egg who the Empress would have personally trusted to oversee her tributes, before they were adopted as a V\u2019neef?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in second edition <i>he</i> was Fleet Admiral V'Neef Ririon. (Compass: Blessed Isle.) However, details have changed between editions. So...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T05:27:56-07:00","id":1382128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382078#post1382078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given everything else Ragara has gotten up to and the way the timeline sets that up, I honestly find that very suspicious. It would not surprise me one bit to discover that Ragara framed them up and down in order to get his own house. Or that he was behind them getting Eyem. Or that Eyem is now in HIS basement giving him solid financial advice, because he cooked the books so everyone would think it was an evil mastermind.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what WFHW says (p. 58) about House Ragara, Eyem probably isn't even the weirdest or most dangerous thing in his basement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T06:00:12-07:00","id":1382139,"title":"","content":"I wonder though if Ragara was always into dark occult stuff, or that's a later thing, as he became desperate to achieve his aim of being named Heir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T12:11:28-07:00","id":1382217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382128#post1382128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what WFHW says (p. 58) about House Ragara, Eyem probably isn't even the weirdest or most dangerous thing in his basement.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e canon the Empress ended up with Eyem in her basement.<br /> Personally, I always speculated that Ragara as having a lingering distrust of artifical consiousness which would make Szaya and Kes' development of Icemind a risky move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T12:18:18-07:00","id":1382220,"title":"","content":"I do appreciate that not every AI in Exalted is treated as an unbeatable runaway thing with complete control. Some of them are a bit dangerous, but not necessarily moreso that the dangerous people in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T00:46:33-07:00","id":1382294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382088#post1382088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don\u2019t have an identity on the Admiral of the Merchant fleet, do we?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s a V\u2019neef, though probably (given the very high rank and responsibility, and the age of the House) an adopted one? Presumably a former Found Egg who the Empress would have personally trusted to oversee her tributes, before they were adopted as a V\u2019neef?</div> </div> </div> </div>V'neef's profile finally brought it home to me how largely arbitrary (or solely down to V'Neef's aspect alone) that house's historic designation as a Wood has to be in practicality. Sure, the founder is a Wood aspect, maybe most of her less than a handful of children that Exalt are, but the overwhelming majority, the adoptees? <br /> <br /> I mean, it'd require someone sitting there and going, casting style, 'You... you... NOT YOU...' through the lost eggs suitable for adoption, looking for wood aspects...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T02:54:14-07:00","id":1382301,"title":"","content":"True, but most houses are only about 40 % the same Aspect anyway. Partly because most dynasts have fathers from other houses, partly because that's just how Dragonblood work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T10:14:04-07:00","id":1382342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382294#post1382294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V'neef's profile finally brought it home to me how largely arbitrary (or solely down to V'Neef's aspect alone) that house's historic designation as a Wood has to be in practicality. Sure, the founder is a Wood aspect, maybe most of her less than a handful of children that Exalt are, but the overwhelming majority, the adoptees? <br /> <br /> I mean, it'd require someone sitting there and going, casting style, 'You... you... NOT YOU...' through the lost eggs suitable for adoption, looking for wood aspects...</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Houses have all 5 Aspects, but the Realm does have a cultural bias toward matching elemental associations (I.e. Dragon-Blooded men are more likely to marry women of Houses that are associated with their Aspect, thus promoting that element in the children of said House). Just like how Dynasts and Lookshy DBs are most likely to wield artifacts of their associated color jade, though there is no mechanics reason for that (I add the cultural note that Prasad does the opposite, culturally favoring mixing the elements).<br /> <br /> That said, yeah V\u2019neef is probably closer to elementally balanced than any House other than Nellens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-18-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T10:16:31-07:00","id":1382344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382301#post1382301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but most houses are only about 40 % the same Aspect anyway. Partly because most dynasts have fathers from other houses, partly because that's just how Dragonblood work.</div> </div> </div> </div>40% still requires a pretty strong amount of \u201cmarry the fire aspected Cynis boy to a Seuss\u201d, or else the plurality of any given element would vanish over enough time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T11:21:36-07:00","id":1382353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382344#post1382344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 40% still requires a pretty strong amount of \u201cmarry the fire aspected Cynis boy to a Seuss\u201d, or else the plurality of any given element would vanish over enough time.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a bit of fun, wonder which, if there was such a thing, secondary aspect each of the Great Houses most exemplify?<br /> <br /> Thinking Earth for Tepet and Cathak (war), maybe air for Mnemom (lore). Ragara... water for bureaucracy and larceny?<br /> <br /> Peleps are swashbucklers now, maybe fire? Sesus... water?<br /> <br /> Any more for any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-18-2020, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T11:32:04-07:00","id":1382358,"title":"","content":"Water for V'neef, fire for Cynis. Dunno on Ledaal. Nellens give me water vibes (adaptable), Iselsi... dunno. Air for stealth maybe.<br /> <br /> Haven't made anyone wood...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:53:58-07:00","id":1382371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382358#post1382358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water for V'neef, fire for Cynis. Dunno on Ledaal. Nellens give me water vibes (adaptable), Iselsi... dunno. Air for stealth maybe.<br /> <br /> Haven't made anyone wood...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to give them secondaries it'd be:<br /> <br /> Cathak - Air, due to their kind of high brow idealization, emphasis on tactics, and so on.<br /> <br /> Cynis - Water due to their mercantile emphasis, blackmail system, and general duplicitous stuff going on.<br /> <br /> Ledaal - Earth. They're very conservative, very much about keeping the Realm stable, and very much about order.<br /> <br /> Mnemon - Honestly it's the Earthiest of Earth Houses to Earth, but if I were to give it something IT hink Fire. Mnemon as a house has a lot of drive to excellence, seems to have folks put passion into their work and there's a good maount of just being the best/most to it that feels FIrey to me.<br /> <br /> Nellens - It kind of does have a bit of everything. It has Water for flexibility, Wood of rwnat to grow, and Fire due to drive. One of those, but since it has no particujlar Aspect now I think that hte fact htey all fit is why.<br /> <br /> Peleps - Fire. There's a lot of drive/passion/pride going on in that house. The long term domination of the Navy, and the fact they had this drive to set off and foudn their won empire for years now to me indicates that too.<br /> <br /> Ragara - Water. The House has a lot of this &quot;hidden depths&quot; theme going to it. There is a large investment on bureaucracy and finance, and they also have a pretty big invsigative wing.<br /> <br /> Sesus - Water. Their skullduggary kind fo fits that.<br /> <br /> Tepet - Earth. They have a big traditonal streak, have ancient roots, and seemed until recently pretty stable/consistent a place to be.<br /> <br /> V'Neef - Water probably due to just drawing in a lot of Water Aspects to help with the Merchant Fleet when it was formed. It also fits with the house's general flexiblity thing.<br /> <br /> Iselsi - Wood actually. It has this &quot;survive at all costs, do what you can all costs, adapt&quot; thing. Kind of an inverse of V'Neef in a way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T01:40:48-07:00","id":1382470,"title":"","content":"Liking all of these.<br /> <br /> I had the greatest problem with placing Ledaal, they're very air, but earth makes sense. I was thinking wood maybe to reflect medicine and biological experiments on shikari.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T02:06:43-07:00","id":1382481,"title":"","content":"So, Samathi Anja, Anja Silverclaws, and Anjei Marama - how many more &quot;Anj-&quot; named ladies are there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T11:46:23-07:00","id":1382562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382481#post1382481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Samathi Anja, Anja Silverclaws, and Anjei Marama - how many more &quot;Anj-&quot; named ladies are there?</div> </div> </div> </div>The outcaste Wood Aspect Rutanjali? Or were you just going for the start of the name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:10:11-07:00","id":1382580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382353#post1382353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a bit of fun, wonder which, if there was such a thing, secondary aspect each of the Great Houses most exemplify?<br /> <br /> Thinking Earth for Tepet and Cathak (war), maybe air for Mnemom (lore). Ragara... water for bureaucracy and larceny?<br /> <br /> Peleps are swashbucklers now, maybe fire? Sesus... water?<br /> <br /> Any more for any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc in 2e canon House Mnemon dynasts exalted as Air Aspects enough it was considered something like a secondary aspect for the house (and something that would normally speak negatively on a house's breeding, though less so in Mnemon's case). I think the person who suggested Fire for them has good points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","user":"tumbleweed664","date":". 04-19-2020, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:48:28-07:00","id":1382739,"title":"","content":"You can't give Nellens a secondary aspect because that would just be their primary aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T09:19:12-07:00","id":1382773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382739#post1382739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't give Nellens a secondary aspect because that would just be their primary aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You speak the truth. Do feel like Water is a decent shout for where they are heading, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> says, they deliberately embody lots of things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T03:52:52-07:00","id":1382944,"title":"","content":"This is sounding like a very cool book. Any backers wanna share some favorite bits with us fools who didn't back?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to picture a windblade. Someone earlier compared them to motorcycles you can ram into people with? Are you normally, like, chucking a motorcycle at people? I'm intrigued...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4620-tumbleweed664","name":"tumbleweed664","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:14:12-07:00","id":1382949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382944#post1382944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is sounding like a very cool book. Any backers wanna share some favorite bits with us fools who didn't back?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to picture a windblade. Someone earlier compared them to motorcycles you can ram into people with? Are you normally, like, chucking a motorcycle at people? I'm intrigued...</div> </div> </div> </div>Think more of a <b>flying surfboard</b>. Windblades are described as narrow, aerodynamic platforms, of magic material and solidified essence, a yard across when expanded, that allow an attuned wielder to fly while standing atop them (5 motes for each hour). They can also be collapsed to the size of a heavy belt buckle for storage.<br /> <br /> Blazerider is a Red Jade Windblade (Artifact \u00a7\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), with some sweet firey evocations. It is currently in still the hands of House Ferem of Cherak. \u2026<i>currently</i>...<br /> <br /> <b>Flying Dragon's Fang</b>, the evocation that allows Blazerider to be wielded as a thrown weapon, also allows it to be thrown while flying on it (the user then falls one range band before it returns to catch them). That, and a few of the other evocations (including the well named essence 4 capstone <b>Devastating Fire-Vortex Blitz</b>) make it one hot ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-21-2020, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:37:42-07:00","id":1382954,"title":"","content":"I assumed it was something like this:<br /> <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/warhammer40k/images/6/6b/DarkEldarHellion2.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/147?cb=20120624024505\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20120624024505</a><br /> <br /> Or this:<br /> <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/villains/images/b/ba/Green-Goblin-Norman-Osborn-Marvel-Comics-Spider-Man-h167.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20161119141455\" target=\"_blank\">https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/...20161119141455</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:21:13-07:00","id":1382960,"title":"","content":"Windblade 2E stats from Wonder of the Lost Age:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">WINDBLADE-CLASS PERSONAL TRANSPORT<br /> (ARTIFACT \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Repair: 3<br /> The smallest skyship model produced in the First Age, the Windblade-class personal transport normally appears as a heavy metal chevron the size of a large belt buckle. Attuning this device costs only one committed mote. When thrown or dropped by an attuned bearer who spends an additional 10 motes (uncommitted), the device slows and hovers in midair, unfurling cunningly articulated plates to <br /> form a narrow, angular platform roughly a yard long. <br /> The device\u2019s master can step up onto this platform with one foot ahead of the other on marked control pads at any time in this configuration, triggering enchantments that make the personal transport adhere to her feet and prevent falling. <br /> <br /> The device is piloted with the feet, leaving the user\u2019s hands free to hold weapons or perform other tasks. During the First Age, archers equipped with these transports used them as mobile sniping platforms above a battlefi eld. While flying or hovering, these craft emit an oscillating hum. They must be fed 10 motes by their user every hour, or they slowly fall to <br /> the ground and retract back into their portable state. <br /> A few particularly exotic daiklaves can unfurl into Windblade craft. Such daiklaves are rated Artifact 4, and have the statistics of normal daiklaves while not in flight mode. Attuning such a device requires the usual five motes instead of one.<br /> <br /> Additional properties of a Windblade-class transport <br /> depend on the magical material used in its construction:<br /> <br /> Orichalcum: These models are faster, with a Speed <br /> of 50/100mph.<br /> Moonsilver: These models are more nimble and re-<br /> sponsive, with Maneuverability 7.<br /> Starmetal: These models weave and dip across the <br /> skeins of fate as well as air, adding two to the Dodge DV of craft and pilot beyond normal.<br /> Jade: Built exclusively of blue jade, these models have small integrated cannons that fire lightning pulses from a forward-facing spur mounted on the underside. Each blast costs the pilot five motes and has the following statistics: <br /> Speed 6, Accuracy (pilot\u2019s Dexterity + Archery), Damage (8L or 12B) piercing, Range 100, Rate 1. Variant models have an integrated elemental lens instead.<br /> Soulsteel: At will, the pilot can extend jagged blades <br /> like bat wings from each side of the craft. The pilot attacks by \u201cramming\u201d opponents with these blades as a Speed 5, Rate 2 attack. The craft takes no damage from this ramming, but the target suffers 10L + attack successes. Opponents killed by these blades are typically beheaded or cut in half.<br /> <br /> Speed: 34/70mph<br /> Maneuverability: +4R (Lore 1, Ride 3)<br /> Endurance: Consumes 10 motes per hour; suffers one level <br /> of unsoakable bashing damage for every 50 cumulative hours <br /> of operation since last maintenance.<br /> Crew: 1/1<br /> Cargo: Pilot\u2019s personal possessions only. Particularly heavy loads, such as a pilot carrying a second person in her arms, halve Speed and apply a -3 Maneuverability penalty.<br /> Armor: 10L/15B<br /> Health Levels: Ux7/Mx4/Cx3/I/D<br /> Weapons: Usually none; jade and soulsteel models have weapons as noted.<br /> Other Notes: Characters flying on a Windblade-class personal transport are treated as holding a tower shield (see Exalted, p. 377), but this protection is not compatible with other shields or cover (only the best value applies). A piloted transport and its pilot both have a Dodge DV equal to ([the pilot\u2019s Dexterity + Ride + Essence + craft\u2019s Maneuverability] \u00f7 2), and the pilot may use her Parry DV to defend against <br /> attacks launched at her vehicle or herself.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Obviously the 3E presentation is quite different. But I hope that wets an appetite. I don't recall offhand if Windblades appeared in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T06:00:04-07:00","id":1382964,"title":"","content":"I always pictured windblades like the Green Goblin's glider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T19:55:31-07:00","id":1383078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382944#post1382944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is sounding like a very cool book. Any backers wanna share some favorite bits with us fools who didn't back?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to picture a windblade. Someone earlier compared them to motorcycles you can ram into people with? Are you normally, like, chucking a motorcycle at people? I'm intrigued...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just compared it to a motorcycle because I was trying to analogize it to action movies, because the charm Flying Dragon's Fang reminded me of one. I guess I figured you be more likely to do that in an action movie with a flying motorcycle in a movie then a green goblin glider type thing - not sure what that was based on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T09:47:52-07:00","id":1383155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382964#post1382964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always pictured windblades like the Green Goblin's glider.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a picture in Wonders of the Lost Age, and the artist seems to have agreed with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:44:52-07:00","id":1383180,"title":"","content":"Windblades are sort of a combination of the Green Goblin's Glider, flying surfboards, and the vague idea that Solar Cloud Strife really ought to be able to fly around by standing on the Buster Sword. Like, &quot;Flying blade you fly on, point forward,&quot; and &quot;Flying blade you fly on, but sideways so the edges are beside your feet&quot; is not something that needs to be written up as two different artifacts; you can just have one artifact category where some are shaped like the former and some are shaped like the latter, and you decide which one yours is and it helps shape which stunts you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:48:15-07:00","id":1383181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383180#post1383180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Windblades are sort of a combination of the Green Goblin's Glider, flying surfboards, and the vague idea that Solar Cloud Strife really ought to be able to fly around by standing on the Buster Sword. Like, &amp;quot;Flying blade you fly on, point forward,&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Flying blade you fly on, but sideways so the edges are beside your feet&amp;quot; is not something that needs to be written up as two different artifacts; you can just have one artifact category where some are shaped like the former and some are shaped like the latter, and you decide which one yours is and it helps shape which stunts you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would anything break if it\u2019s the same artifact and you can just fly it in either position?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:50:53-07:00","id":1383182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383181#post1383181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would anything break if it\u2019s the same artifact and you can just fly it in either position?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered how an artifact magic broom ala Harry Potter might be statted and classified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T12:04:23-07:00","id":1383185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383181#post1383181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would anything break if it\u2019s the same artifact and you can just fly it in either position?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think so, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:58:15-07:00","id":1383209,"title":"","content":"I really like Prasad, the Forest Witches, the Cult of the Violet Fang and Heaven's Dragons. I'm currently working on a character whose backstory will include all of those somehow. :-D<br /> Moon and Earth marriage made me squeal in glee. It's going in the backstory too!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:18:27-07:00","id":1383219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383209#post1383209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Prasad, the Forest Witches, the Cult of the Violet Fang and Heaven's Dragons. I'm currently working on a character whose backstory will include all of those somehow. :-D<br /> Moon and Earth marriage made me squeal in glee. It's going in the backstory too!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love the sample character descriptions for Heaven\u2019s Dragons, but for my own table, it just seems too subservient a position for DBs, when they could be exercising the Creation Ruling Mandate and are choosing not to for some reason.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll likely reimagine those listed characters as God-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T15:56:55-07:00","id":1383240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tumbleweed664</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1382944#post1382944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is sounding like a very cool book. Any backers wanna share some favorite bits with us fools who didn't back?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to picture a windblade. Someone earlier compared them to motorcycles you can ram into people with? Are you normally, like, chucking a motorcycle at people? I'm intrigued...</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to reply to this earlier, but the talk of wielding a motorcycle as a weapon directly led to the fianc\u00e9e and I fondly recalling The One and ultimately deciding to rewatch it.<br /> <br /> I regret nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T17:31:43-07:00","id":1383247,"title":"","content":"I'm in a space where I can see why, conceptually, Gunzosha armor essentially ate the Five Dragon Armors and Celestial Battle Armor, and would consider retrofitting that into past editions, but it still feels kind of weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T22:20:56-07:00","id":1383292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383247#post1383247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in a space where I can see why, conceptually, Gunzosha armor essentially ate the Five Dragon Armors and Celestial Battle Armor, and would consider retrofitting that into past editions, but it still feels kind of weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly we still need at least 7 or 8 more examples of Gunzosha armor!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T22:29:05-07:00","id":1383294,"title":"","content":"If we take the theme of 3e that all 3 dots+ artifacts are unique, the difference between the Gunzosha armor are really just which evocations a character unlock and since by the lore established in Arms of the Chosen, evocations unlocked are considered unique to a character...beside the standard 3 Gunzosha evocations, everybody has a different Gunzosha armor now with their own unique quirks/perks and evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:42:26-07:00","id":1383333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383219#post1383219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the sample character descriptions for Heaven\u2019s Dragons, but for my own table, it just seems too subservient a position for DBs, when they could be exercising the Creation Ruling Mandate and are choosing not to for some reason.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll likely reimagine those listed characters as God-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mostly took this to mean than even living in the slums of Heaven seemed preferable than living in Creation for them. I like the idea of them having a broader view on the history of Creation and of the Dragon-Blooded host. I especially like the idea of them infiltrating the Dynasty or other Dragon-Blooded society for in service to some Heavenly patron and potentially bringing a truly distant perspective on Dragon-Blooded affairs and conflicts.<br /> But they don't need to be subservient; Some Dragon-Blooded families being Heaven's Mafia is specifically mentionned. Others families have developped legal family businesses that have endured millenia and as such have had much time to grow and become potentially enormous. There could be a Dragon-Blooded version (or more) of Jeff Bezos or Bill Gates with their own financial empire in Yu-Shan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:46:56-07:00","id":1383334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383294#post1383294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we take the theme of 3e that all 3 dots+ artifacts are unique, the difference between the Gunzosha armor are really just which evocations a character unlock and since by the lore established in Arms of the Chosen, evocations unlocked are considered unique to a character...beside the standard 3 Gunzosha evocations, everybody has a different Gunzosha armor now with their own unique quirks/perks and evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much. Although on FAA you often find evocations that represent actual physical systems (such as the standard gunzosha ones) and presumably those would be consistent between wearers even if they're unique to the armour itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T06:00:48-07:00","id":1383346,"title":"","content":"Re: Windblades<br /> <br /> What about Eureka Seven? Seems like a good inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media1.tenor.com/images/69240b8b36c662a1904c22976eb42092/tenor.gif?itemid=11413432\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T06:21:07-07:00","id":1383355,"title":"","content":"I am so uncool. For windblades my brain just goes here: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YqLr0Qy-DyE?t=54\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/YqLr0Qy-DyE?t=54</a><br /> <br /> In my defence, it is a <i>great</i> theme tune...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:37:29-07:00","id":1383374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383219#post1383219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the sample character descriptions for Heaven\u2019s Dragons, but for my own table, it just seems too subservient a position for DBs, when they could be exercising the Creation Ruling Mandate and are choosing not to for some reason.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ll likely reimagine those listed characters as God-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Heavens Dragons diverged from my expectations too.<br /> <br /> In this presentation they mostly feel like Outcastes who somehow found their way into Yu-Shan like Gemstone Ocean Hero did with Malfeas, in that sense they are not any more subservient than a Terrestrial serving as hired muscle for a Guild Prince. However, I am not really getting the sense that they are decendents of Dragon-Blooded who moved there immediately after the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>To clarify, I strongly suspect I know why they differ from my expectations. In that this is a suppliment for Dragon-Blooded not a Yu-Shan and has no particular interest in dwelling on the culture of these insular enclaves of mortals and Dragon-Blooded that have in some ways been seperated from Creation longer than Autochthonia, and who will not be encountered outside of Yu-Shan. Instead focusing on the possibility for the player characters becoming involved in something like smuggling things into Yu-Shan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","user":"Bastet","date":". 04-23-2020, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:03:13-07:00","id":1383402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383334#post1383334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, pretty much. Although on FAA you often find evocations that represent actual physical systems (such as the standard gunzosha ones) and presumably those would be consistent between wearers even if they're unique to the armour itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>FAA is not so much about aesthetic in itself. That mortals can use them adn they have the unified Evocations is what makes them FAA. How those manifest can be as magitechy or not. Even what a &quot;physical system&quot; is might not look quite the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:29:05-07:00","id":1383405,"title":"","content":"I liked the Heaven's Dragons. An improvement on 2e definitely. I didn't find them amazing, but good. Not every single Dragonblood game has to be about theo-aristocrats who are at the top of the social pyramid I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:35:09-07:00","id":1383407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383405#post1383405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Heaven's Dragons. An improvement on 2e definitely. I didn't find them amazing, but good. Not every single Dragonblood game has to be about theo-aristocrats who are at the top of the social pyramid I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Astonished monocle dropping noise*<br /> <br /> I <i>say</i>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T13:05:19-07:00","id":1383428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383355#post1383355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so uncool. For windblades my brain just goes here: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YqLr0Qy-DyE?t=54\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/YqLr0Qy-DyE?t=54</a><br /> <br /> In my defence, it is a <i>great</i> theme tune...</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Ducktales reboot keeps doing well, they've already planted the seed for Tail Spin being part of its universe.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I always thought of Kit Cloudkicker and his air foil when I thought of windblades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T00:22:33-07:00","id":1383524,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's the right place to ask, but how spirit-like are the numina? Anja seems not to age, but could she or the others summon a demon or elemental through sorcery? Could they get their own sanctums or steal a god's? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T03:04:39-07:00","id":1383546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383524#post1383524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's the right place to ask, but how spirit-like are the numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are spirits as well as exalts. They are material by default, but may Dematerialise. The revive within the Mists after a month if slain without <i>magic</i> capable of permakilling spirits. They hear prayers directed to them. How spirit like is that?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383524#post1383524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anja seems not to age, but could she or the others summon a demon or elemental through sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is no prohibition on spirits learning sorcery; but most just do not. However, Numina are exalts as well as spirits, so may access sorcery and learn spells as Dragonblooded do. So why not?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383524#post1383524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could they get their own sanctums or steal a god's?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Maybe?</i> It is uncertain how Sanctums work in third edition. <i>However</i> I'd say that the Mist takes on that role for the Numina, and it would at least be inappropriate for a Numen to occupy a sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:39:11-07:00","id":1383579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383405#post1383405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Heaven's Dragons. An improvement on 2e definitely. I didn't find them amazing, but good. Not every single Dragonblood game has to be about theo-aristocrats who are at the top of the social pyramid I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like them too. My critique is that the presentation suffers from the lack of something analogous to Great Houses, Gentes or Clans for these several millennia old family units that leaves some of the NPCs feeling a little disconnected from an interesting part of their premise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T06:07:01-07:00","id":1383585,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a fair point. Even just one or two as an example.<br /> Hmmm... how many are they? Maybe with the small number of Dragonblood in Heaven, they've all been marrying each other and so basically are one family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T06:50:19-07:00","id":1383593,"title":"","content":"No numbers given.<br /> The implication is certainly that there are multiple families living in their own predominently mortal enclave communities in the slums of Yu-Shan. Even if there is a lack of genetic diversity I would imagine indvidual enclaves would be characterised by their own challenges.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:46:29-07:00","id":1383606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383524#post1383524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's the right place to ask, but how spirit-like are the numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>They count as spirits for things that say &quot;spirits.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anja seems not to age, but could she or the others summon a demon or elemental through sorcery? </div> </div> </div>Yes; the &quot;being an Exalt&quot; part trumps the &quot;being a spirit part&quot; with regard to that limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could they get their own sanctums or steal a god's? </div> </div> </div>Numina don't naturally have sanctums, but they could steal someone else's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:28:19-07:00","id":1383614,"title":"","content":"How much xp do mortals pay for evocations from gunzosha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:40:54-07:00","id":1383624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383614#post1383614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much xp do mortals pay for evocations from gunzosha?</div> </div> </div> </div>12 apiece (that was omitted from the preview, but it's been added).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T10:48:15-07:00","id":1383627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383405#post1383405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Heaven's Dragons. An improvement on 2e definitely. I didn't find them amazing, but good. Not every single Dragonblood game has to be about theo-aristocrats who are at the top of the social pyramid I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in theory, but I also think that if a niche can be better filled by some other character type it should be, and FOR MY TABLE, I think God-Blooded and the occasional Exigent fit those described character niches better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:26:34-07:00","id":1383653,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure, god-bloods can definitely fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:44:48-07:00","id":1383659,"title":"","content":"I think that Heaven's Dragons live in Heaven and aren't treated like trash instinctively by all the gods there isn't a bad start though. I could see more on them in anything dealing wiht Heaven later might be a good idea though. But Heaven to me feels like a place that humans live and DBs happen to Exalt amongst thsoe humans, rather than being a place with DB lineages there, which I can see the feel that htey don't feel as like a legacy thing. Though that said, those Exalts then getting good jobs working in the Celestial Bureacracy or becoming Divine PIs or Shadowrunners ro whatever ain't bad either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:44:50-07:00","id":1383660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383606#post1383606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They count as spirits for things that say &quot;spirits.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I use Carnal Spirit Rending after killing a Numen with Ghost-Eating Technique, can I access their DB charms? Since CSR isn't limited to Eclipse powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T16:52:52-07:00","id":1383686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383660#post1383660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if I use Carnal Spirit Rending after killing a Numen with Ghost-Eating Technique, can I access their DB charms? Since CSR isn't limited to Eclipse powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Carnal Spirit Rending doesn't let you use specific Charms; it provides &quot;powers or traits based on the Charms and themes of the destroyed spirit, to be decided by the Storyteller.&quot; This could conceivably draw on Dragon-Blooded themes if that strikes the Storyteller's fancy, although I would personally expect to lean toward the specific thematics of the numen in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T03:22:55-07:00","id":1383745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383606#post1383606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They count as spirits for things that say &quot;spirits.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes; the &quot;being an Exalt&quot; part trumps the &quot;being a spirit part&quot; with regard to that limitation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Numina don't naturally have sanctums, but they could steal someone else's.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answers!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T17:20:23-07:00","id":1383875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383624#post1383624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">12 apiece (that was omitted from the preview, but it's been added).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are the standard gunzosha armor evocations immediately unlocked on attunement, or do they need to be purchased?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T18:06:09-07:00","id":1383882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383875#post1383875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the standard gunzosha armor evocations immediately unlocked on attunement, or do they need to be purchased?</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, all universal gunzosha evocations need to be purchased to unlock. Gunzosha must work hard to master their armour's features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-25-2020, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T11:29:10-07:00","id":1383982,"title":"","content":"Related question: If you unlock a standard evocation on one suit, should you need to unlock the same evocation on a different suit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:38:10-07:00","id":1384076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383982#post1383982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question: If you unlock a standard evocation on one suit, should you need to unlock the same evocation on a different suit?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting question, but it does not say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:30:20-07:00","id":1384089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1383982#post1383982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question: If you unlock a standard evocation on one suit, should you need to unlock the same evocation on a different suit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that by strict RAW, each artifact's Evocations are different and would have to be bought separately. However, if I were STing I would allow Evocations purchased on one artifact to be applied to the other as well (perhaps after a brief training and familiarization period) when they're the <i>exact same Evocation</i>, as in this case.<br /> <br /> (For the same reason, if someone used Courante for a while and then picked up Galliard instead for some reason, as long as they paid XP for Argent Defender first I'd allow them to use all the matching Evocations they'd unlocked from Courante.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:19:24-07:00","id":1384215,"title":"","content":"Given that absolutely every artifact considered Gunzosha armor always shares the same four basic Evocations by definition, it only makes sense that mastery of any those shared Evocations in one would be applicable to all others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would anyone consider the Doomslayer's Praetor Armor to be Gunzosha, or simply heavy artifact armor?<br /> <br /> His armor in <i>Doom: Eternal</i> doesn't seem to be powered-armor, since it leaves his upper arms bare. No exoskeletal strength, there, though the armor might have it in the lower body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:57:00-07:00","id":1384256,"title":"","content":"I'm away from my copy of the documents, but I feel I'm right about this:<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to have a normal artifact armor with any of the four basic Gunzosha Evocations, or with &quot;unique&quot; and characteristic Evocations that basically do the same thing as any of those. The major differences being that mortals cannot use such armor, and the armor being easier to build and repair.<br /> <br /> Aesthetically speaking, there need be no other differences. It could still be &quot;powered-armor&quot;, just with such demanding costs that mortals cannot suffice even with the implants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:14:30-07:00","id":1384905,"title":"","content":"My one concern reading this book is the implied upcoming war between Ysyr and Prasad. The two empires (at least so far as I know) are thousands of miles apart, and I fear that this is a repeat of 2E where Cities in the Core have these relationships with each other as if there's no other nations in between them. (Lookshy and the Haslanti comes to mind.)<br /> <br /> Looking at <a href=\"https://www.loom3e.com/map/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.loom3e.com/map/</a>, the distance is ~3750 miles. This is Rome to Delhi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 04-30-2020, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T13:32:36-07:00","id":1384909,"title":"","content":"True, but it is at least a battle over the seas (where people travel faster), and IIRC it's a war over Y'danna, which is in the middle between them? A bit less than 1000 miles from each.<br /> It's a much shorter distance than, say, the Crusades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T15:22:02-07:00","id":1384937,"title":"","content":"Kind of worth looking that Prasad is pretty lopsided an empire too. It probably has a lot of clients tates on the way (which could turn and cause issues if stuff gets strained enough) and it's probably looks like Mali more than it does Rome when it comes to where the capital is in relation ot the rest of it. I kind of imagine this, mirorred, and Kamthahar where Timbuktu or even Gao is. Y'Danna woudl be somewhere around where the Gambia is on the map in relation, which isn't too weird.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/MALI_empire_map.PNG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:59:09-07:00","id":1385190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1384905#post1384905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one concern reading this book is the implied upcoming war between Ysyr and Prasad. The two empires (at least so far as I know) are thousands of miles apart, and I fear that this is a repeat of 2E where Cities in the Core have these relationships with each other as if there's no other nations in between them. (Lookshy and the Haslanti comes to mind.)<br /> <br /> Looking at <a href=\"https://www.loom3e.com/map/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.loom3e.com/map/</a>, the distance is ~3750 miles. This is Rome to Delhi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth stressing here that there isn\u2019t any chance of Prasad conquering Ysyr here, or Ysyr taking Kamthahar. Think of it more as Rome v Parthia, where the outer limits of the respective empires clashed, and in this case they share a sea.<br /> <br /> Previous editions presentation of Halta v Linnowans never made sense because it was an all encompassing existential war between cultures that defined themselves at odds with each other - which is nonsense given their distance. But two empires having a purely strategic control of a given sea based conflict can make sense at those distances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-02-2020, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T22:01:15-07:00","id":1385191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1384937#post1384937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of worth looking that Prasad is pretty lopsided an empire too. It probably has a lot of clients tates on the way (which could turn and cause issues if stuff gets strained enough) and it's probably looks like Mali more than it does Rome when it comes to where the capital is in relation ot the rest of it. I kind of imagine this, mirorred, and Kamthahar where Timbuktu or even Gao is. Y'Danna woudl be somewhere around where the Gambia is on the map in relation, which isn't too weird.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/MALI_empire_map.PNG\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah that works provided a major river flowing from the Summer Mountains to the Dreaming Sea serves as a major spine for their empire, the way the Niger did for Mali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T00:12:20-07:00","id":1385207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1385190#post1385190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worth stressing here that there isn\u2019t any chance of Prasad conquering Ysyr here, or Ysyr taking Kamthahar. Think of it more as Rome v Parthia, where the outer limits of the respective empires clashed, and in this case they share a sea.<br /> <br /> Previous editions presentation of Halta v Linnowans never made sense because it was an all encompassing existential war between cultures that defined themselves at odds with each other - which is nonsense given their distance. But two empires having a purely strategic control of a given sea based conflict can make sense at those distances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... Halta and Linowan border each other? It's just that Halta was ludicrously big.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are examples, but I don't think that's a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T00:45:08-07:00","id":1385210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1385207#post1385207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... Halta and Linowan border each other? It's just that Halta was ludicrously big.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are examples, but I don't think that's a good one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say they didn\u2019t border each other, I was speaking of the distance between their capitals meaning they\u2019d have to both be vast empires, and the actual bordering cultural groups wouldn\u2019t be the Linnowans and Haltans themselves if we were looking at it realistically.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t a problem with Prasad and Ysyr because they actually are supposed to be imperial powers having a territorial control conflict, and not two bordering culture groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-02-2020, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T01:04:54-07:00","id":1385212,"title":"","content":"Ah, that makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:45:56-07:00","id":1385741,"title":"","content":"Has it ever been clearly defined in what main direction Prasad extends? I've never been quite sure whether it runs north, northeast, or east from Kamthahar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:06:50-07:00","id":1385752,"title":"","content":"I assume that Kamthahar is kind of in the middle of Prasad, as capitals often are (but certainly not always).<br /> I do know they've only recently reached the coast of the Dreaming Sea, so it certainly does extend east to the sea, but I guess not south-east along the coastline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:51:02-07:00","id":1385757,"title":"","content":"With everything that is going on I only just now managed to get to reading part of this. I am incredibly happy they devoted an outcast concept to kicking that Compass of Celestial Direction: Yu-Shan side panel on how 'all gods <i>without exception</i> instinctively loathe and disrespect DBs in the same way we humans instinctively know up from down and considers them lower then humans because at least humans might one day become a real exalt' in the trash where it belongs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-05-2020, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:01:45-07:00","id":1385758,"title":"","content":"Reviewing Lookshy lore.... the city proper should really be further inland on the river if it doesn\u2019t have a protective bay. I get that it\u2019s a military city meant to defend the river\u2019s mouth, but WOW are it\u2019s docks going to be dangerously exposed. You\u2019d think they\u2019d keep forts on either bank of the mouth, and the docks and city proper would be defensible upstream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T00:06:56-07:00","id":1385759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1385741#post1385741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been clearly defined in what main direction Prasad extends? I've never been quite sure whether it runs north, northeast, or east from Kamthahar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm states that the empire stretches from deserts west of the Summer Mountains to the Dreaming Sea's tip, with expanding borders. However, Heirs notes that expansion of the South East borders have been blocked for decades by the Tiger's Nest Coalition, so their recent focus has been on building up naval power.<br /> <br /> The maps don't show borders, but the Jade Road is indicated which runs south-west to north-east through Kamthahar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T02:35:31-07:00","id":1385786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1385759#post1385759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm states that the empire stretches from deserts west of the Summer Mountains</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that part surprised me.<br /> <br /> I think it was mentioned that Across the Eight Directions would have regional maps with more detail, so probably that'll make it clearer. Even if there's no borders (pre-modern borders are often a bit misleading. Hey, modern borders can be misleading at times), you'll probably be able to see lots of places that you know are in or not in Prasad.<br /> <br /> Champoor isn't part of Prasad, is it? They're planning to try conquering it, but haven't yet?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T04:02:55-07:00","id":1385790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377947-heirs-to-the-shogunate-backers-preview-just-dropped?p=1385786#post1385786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that part surprised me.<br /> <br /> I think it was mentioned that Across the Eight Directions would have regional maps with more detail, so probably that'll make it clearer. Even if there's no borders (pre-modern borders are often a bit misleading. Hey, modern borders can be misleading at times), you'll probably be able to see lots of places that you know are in or not in Prasad.<br /> <br /> Champoor isn't part of Prasad, is it? They're planning to try conquering it, but haven't yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, Champoor and Y'danna are both free of Prasad","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com